WEBVTT

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.660
Goodbye, my friend.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.960
Hiroki!

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.030
Hiroki!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.560
I wonder if I'll be able to
fly like Noah's Ark, too...

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.410
Hiroki!

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.030
I'm high school detective Kudo Shinichi.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.440
I went with old friend and classmate,
Mori Ran, to an amusement park

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:53.280
where I witnessed a suspicious
deal with a man dressed in black!

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.310
I was so absorbed with watching the deal

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:59.320
that I didn't notice a second
man sneak up from behind me!

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.760
He forced me to take a poison,
and when I woke up ...

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.630
... my body had shrunk!

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.830
If they learned Kudo Shinichi was alive,
they might go after me again,

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.770
putting all the people around me in danger!

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.300
Per Dr. Agasa's advice,
I decided to conceal my identity.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:22.240
When Ran asked my name,
I quickly answered, "Edogawa Conan".

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.940
To get information on the men,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.930
I wound up living with Ran
and her detective father.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:33.350
- Ready, everyone?!
- Yeah!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.420
Aside from the Doc, the only one
in this group who knows who I am ...

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:41.290
... is Haibara Ai.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:44.030
She originally worked with the men in black,

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:49.690
but to escape from them, she took
the same poison I did and shrank!

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:11.520
My parents are so childish
and always love to pull pranks.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.830
My dad is the world-renowned
mystery novelist, Kudo Yusaku.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:20.320
There's no mystery fan who hasn't
heard of his Night Baron series!

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:24.400
My mom, Kudo Yukiko,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.970
was a legendary idol actress
who retired at 20 to get married.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.970
She's just an annoying
middle-aged lady now, though.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:38.850
For the time being, I'm a
"distant relative" of theirs.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:44.420
I haven't seen them in a while.
I wonder how my mom and dad are ...

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.420
I'm just dandy!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:51.730
Even when I'm small, my mind
remains that of a sharp detective!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.720
There is always only one truth!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.880
We're here at Beika City Hall,
at the spectacular premier

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.880
of the sensory simulation game
developed by Japanese game makers

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.870
in cooperation with the Schindler Company!

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.020
Oh! President Schindler of the
Schindler Company has just arrived!

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.970
Now, then! According to the
documents distributed to the media,

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:42.280
players enter capsules called "Cocoons"

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:50.290
and interact with virtual reality
worlds while in a hypnotic state

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.760
in this conglomeration of
cutting-edge technology!

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:59.730
This game is said to have five types
of stages the player can enjoy.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.600
Just what kind of virtual
worlds they are will be revealed

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:10.740
when the children at today's
sneak preview play for the first time!

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.780
Fifty boys and girls at
or below high school age

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.770
will be the first in Japan
to experience the Cocoons!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.490
Geez! This is a bit much for some
stupid video game presentation!

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:32.330
I hear they had to put up with corporate
spies and stuff like that just to get this far!

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:38.000
Yeah, the Cocoons are supposed
to change video games forever!

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:42.440
What're those?!

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:45.210
Oh! Are those the Cocoons?!

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.980
I want to play in one ...

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:52.320
I'm afraid you can't.
We were invited to the party,

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:55.550
but we weren't chosen to try the Cocoons.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:09:00.220
But being able to experience actual,
historical events inside the games

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.860
is somewhat interesting.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:02.690
Yeah, huh?!

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:06.660
It'd be like taking a journey
as a real-life time traveler!

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.630
C'mon, it's just a game!

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.800
Oh, yeah. I forgot you're bad
at computer games, <i>Conan-kun.</i>

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.310
Yeah, I can't believe
you're still stuck in Final Quest!

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.680
Yeah, you're surprisingly
not good with your fingers!

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.340
Shut up.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.730
So many people, so much booze!

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:40.160
Dad! Important police officials are here!
Don't drink too much!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:45.000
Yeah, yeah! You can't get
sick from expensive liquor!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.940
That's not what she means ...

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.410
This is all-you-can-eat, right?!

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.740
Yes, probably ...

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.610
Lucky! Lucky!

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.270
Those kids are the lucky ones.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.750
Seeing them receive their
game badges really hits home

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.560
that they're lucky they
get to play today's game ...

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.890
The assistant commissioner's grandson,

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:09.290
a financial big shot's grandson,

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.630
the son of a politician from the ruling party ...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:16.470
Japan's future will be on these <i>guys</i>
shoulders in the next generation!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.370
- I'm sensing jealous looks!
- Yeah!

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.570
It's as if Japan's horrid hereditary system

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.140
has been concentrated in this one location.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:30.550
It's due to that very system that
society repeats its transgressions.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:34.620
<i>Haibara-san,</i> I don't
understand what you're saying.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:38.760
Hey, now! Talk more like a kid!

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.560
Politicians sons will become politicians.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.130
CEO's sons will become CEO's.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:48.120
Japan will never change like this.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:55.090
They said tons of that junk
on the news yesterday, anyway!

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.840
How was that?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.180
Scary ...

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.680
Ran!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.680
Sonoko!

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.320
Hi, boys and girls!

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.120
<i>Sonoko-san!</i> Don't tell me that badge is ...

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.460
Oh, this?

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.130
Are you a chosen one too, Sonoko?!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:19.600
The Suzuki zaibatsu helped fund
the game development, you see.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.270
She's so lucky ...

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.770
I wish I had one ...

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.800
Forget it.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.600
It's not your place.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.610
Were you guys even invited here to begin with?

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:35.810
How rude! I invited these guests myself!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:40.150
Why, hello there,
daughter of the Suzuki Zaibatsu.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:45.960
Listen. People's lives are set in
stone the moment they're born.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:50.630
That's right! Like they say,
"Sharp clothes choose the wearer"!

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:56.700
Those not chosen can simply
look on enviously from the outside.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.670
These creeps really tick me off.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:02.660
Dad! Give them a talking to!

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:11.680
Listen, lads. You mustn't take life lightly.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:16.220
Even the most stable of lives have pitfalls.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:19.860
Someday, when you've become adults,
you will understand this.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.730
Like having your wife run out on you?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.830
I know all about you, old man.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.830
You got the nickname "Sleeping Kogoro"

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:32.830
because your wife left you
while you were asleep, right?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.880
You little brats!

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.410
He wasn't asleep!

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.680
My mom left him while he was in the bathroom!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.010
Right?!

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.620
That's not helping him.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.610
Hey! Let's have a little game!

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:58.700
When I think about kids like them
following their parents footsteps

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.530
and becoming Japan's leaders,
I feel no hope for the future.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:04.860
Agreed.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:15.740
I got it! I got it!

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:23.890
- What's the big idea?!
- Give it back!

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:26.560
You're bothering the other guests.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.890
If you're going to play, take it outside.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.790
And just who are you?

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.430
My name is Kashimura. I was in
charge of the Cocoons development.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.970
It was the money from my dad's
bank that let you finish the game!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:44.980
Have your mothers and fathers not
taught you about public morality

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:49.310
or how to talk to your superiors?

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:50.810
You think you're so great!

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.120
No more money for you!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:56.750
Do you not know who we are, old man?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.990
Defy us, and you might find
yourself without a job tomorrow.

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:07.430
In that case, perhaps I'll throw
you out of here before then.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.760
Let's go.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:17.440
What a cool man!

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.770
Unlike someone else I know.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.070
<i>Shinichi-kun</i> should be here, too.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:49.570
I'm sure you'd like to have
some family time with him.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:53.310
Doc, please keep my relation to him a secret.

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:54.640
Yes, I know.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:59.220
Ladies and gentlemen!
Please turn your attention to the stage!

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:02.220
Kudo <i>Yusaku-sensei</i> has
just arrived from America!

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:06.710
He kindly provided many ideas
used to create the Cocoon games!

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.870
We finally made it back.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.770
You were working with Dad, huh?

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.610
I wondered why you were gone for a month.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.880
I helped out with some
of the final programming.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.040
What about my mom?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:31.580
She hasn't been in Japan for a while,
so she's having a class reunion.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.570
Here. A souvenir for you.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.690
A game participation badge?

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:41.860
I appreciate it, but I can't play it on my own.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:45.200
I think you'd really love it.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.900
It's still a secret ...

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:52.870
... but the game takes place 100 years ago,
in 19th-century London.

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.440
London 100 years ago?!

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:59.480
I see Dad still loves that
setting as much as ever ...

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.470
Like father, like son.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.290
Huh? I can't see a thing ...

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.820
Sorry.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.310
Geez! Don't move around in the darkness!

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.560
Introducing the next generation
gaming machine, the Cocoon!

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.440
This capsule controls the five senses,

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.450
and places players in a realistic world

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:40.920
where everything from touch
to pain to smell are experienced!

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.590
As it electrically acts upon
the central nervous system,

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:46.520
there is no physical damage to the body.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.130
It's no fun just looking ...

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:51.160
Yeah, games are for playing ...

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:54.000
Oh! You're all here!

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.930
In that case, I'll give you a
riddle to pass the boredom!

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:58.300
Eh?!

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:01.840
Not another of the Doc's horrible pun riddles!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:02.940
Should we run for it?

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:06.600
I'm sure he tried hard
thinking it up! Let's hear him out!

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:10.680
Mr. A, an employee of this game company,

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.950
became captivated with
the Cocoon game during work.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:18.360
What did the company
president do after seeing Mr. A?

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:22.960
Did he 1: Award him for finishing the game;

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:26.960
2: Fire him for playing games during work;

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:33.300
or 3: Leave him as-is, since he was
sleeping soundly in the Cocoon.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.470
Number 3! He let him sleep!

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.340
Why's that?

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:40.580
Because the Cocoon looks like a cradle!

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.980
Bzzz!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:44.250
I say it's Number 1, the award!

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.980
That gets a "bzzzz" too!

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.220
Then it's Number 2? How come?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:53.890
I take it you know, <i>Ai-kun?</i>
Could you explain it for them?

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:57.090
I'm wearing light clothing today.
<i>Edogawa-kun</i> can do it.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.230
Eh?

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.760
Sounds like you have a request.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.000
"Cocoon" refers to the insect cocoons.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.740
<i>Kaiko</i> create cocoons. [Silkworms]

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:09.010
And <i>kaiko</i> is another way to say "fire."

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.010
Brr!

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:13.110
I'm gonna get something warm to drink...

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.910
- I'll come with you ...
- Me too ...

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.580
Huh? Is the air conditioning
on too high for them?

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:38.070
These bronze statues are quite magnificent!

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:42.140
I hear they're Mr. Schindler's
favorites from his collection!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:47.140
Oh? He must really like them
to bring them all the way here!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:53.140
Perhaps he shares the fighting
spirit that flows from such statues.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.420
- Uh oh!
- Hideki!

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.560
Quit playing ball inside.

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:04.890
Okay ...

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.730
I guess we screwed up, huh?

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:13.100
It's nothin'. They're all cheap statues.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.440
Are you serious?

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.470
They'd never put anything that expensive here.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:19.510
Yeah, that's true!

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.250
Kashimura Tadaaki, the man in
charge of the Cocoon's development,

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:25.980
was a partner in crime of mine in college,

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:30.490
so I was able to rekindle our old
friendship through this latest job.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.460
Thank you!

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:36.130
This has been Shimizu of TMS!

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.100
Where might I find Kashimura?
I'd like to see him.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:43.170
Right! I'll find him right away!

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.170
<i>Kudo-sensei!</i> Could I have your autograph?!

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:46.500
Me too!

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:55.010
I'm relieved to see you're well.

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:56.340
Likewise.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.490
"Kashimura's Room"

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:31.920
I must return to the conference soon.
Let's make this quick.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:37.590
How much will you sell Hiroki's
"DNA Search Program" for?

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:40.920
I do not intend to extort you.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.590
I simply want you to
atone for what you've done!

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:52.270
Hiroki learned the secret about you
that can ruin the Schindler Empire.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:57.270
But the artificial brain couldn't
be completed without Hiroki's help.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:03.010
You forced Hiroki to work harder to complete it.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:05.550
Having been mentally run ragged,

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:11.250
he believed you would kill him
the instant he finished the brain.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:15.020
That's why he let the Noah's Ark,
practically his electronic double,

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:17.190
escape over the phone lines

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.680
and threw himself over the roof
of that apartment building.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.200
Some time after that,

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:31.270
the DNA Search Program
file snuck onto my computer.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:36.050
It was the doing of Noah's Ark,
acting out Hiroki's will.

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:40.220
It seemed to me like
the scream of Hiroki's soul.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:42.220
I will atone.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:44.320
I will reveal everything to the public,

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.220
and accept whatever judgment I'm given.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:50.560
But, before that, could I
see this DNA Search Program

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:55.230
that Noah's Ark supposedly sent you?

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.890
Very well.

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:21.660
This phantom of London has truly
transcended time, to the modern ...

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:39.820
My name is Noah's Ark.

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:51.880
Sir? <i>Kudo-sensei</i> would like to see you.

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:53.720
Sir?

00:23:53.720 --> 00:23:55.520
Pardon the intrusion, sir.

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:57.850
Sir! What happened?! Sir!

00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:09.470
Now what're they gonna do?

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:11.470
Now, please enjoy this live performance

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:15.310
from our special guest today, Okino <i>Yoko-san!</i>

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:18.470
What?! <i>Yoko-chan's</i> here, too?!

00:24:18.470 --> 00:24:20.970
Those front row seats are mine!

00:24:26.620 --> 00:24:29.490
<i>Chiba-kun,</i> seal all exits.

00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:31.150
Understood!

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:32.960
Attention, all units on standby!

00:24:32.960 --> 00:24:35.490
Many important people
seem to be in attendance.

00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:39.930
Yes. The assistant commissioner,
financial big-wigs,

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:43.330
and even several legislative officials.

00:24:43.330 --> 00:24:46.270
Sounds like we'll have to be especially careful.

00:24:46.270 --> 00:24:48.070
Tadah!

00:24:48.070 --> 00:24:49.470
Whoa!

00:24:49.470 --> 00:24:51.470
Golden Yaiba Cards!

00:24:51.470 --> 00:24:52.910
They're limited edition!

00:24:52.910 --> 00:24:54.610
I want one!

00:24:54.610 --> 00:24:58.080
We'll trade them for your
game badges, if you want!

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.820
But we wanna play the game, too ...

00:25:00.820 --> 00:25:03.320
You can always play the
Cocoons some other day,

00:25:03.320 --> 00:25:08.260
but this might be your only
chance to get a Golden Yaiba Card!

00:25:08.260 --> 00:25:10.660
What do we do?

00:25:10.660 --> 00:25:13.330
Haibara! We got some!

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:15.800
Here! There's one for you, too!

00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:18.460
Oh! How impressive!

00:25:20.270 --> 00:25:23.430
I guess it could make for a
decent conversation piece.

00:25:25.440 --> 00:25:27.430
Excuse me! Please let me through!

00:25:28.540 --> 00:25:31.280
Eh?! Kashimura is?!

00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:34.380
- Please take me there!
- Right!

00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:39.560
Now, then! Let us move to the Cocoon hall!

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:42.550
I don't see Dad anywhere. Where did he go?

00:25:45.190 --> 00:25:47.400
Inspector!

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:50.030
Oh! <i>Mori-kun!</i> You're here, too?

00:25:50.030 --> 00:25:54.670
I saw police cars from the balcony
after my tipsiness wore off, so!

00:25:54.670 --> 00:25:57.570
Wasn't he in charge of
the Cocoons development?

00:25:57.570 --> 00:26:01.980
One stab to the heart.
The weapon was taken from the scene.

00:26:01.980 --> 00:26:04.310
The blood was wiped off ...

00:26:04.310 --> 00:26:06.480
Was the weapon something important?

00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:09.970
Or would it identify the killer if left behind?

00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:17.230
But why would the head of development
work here in the basement?

00:26:17.230 --> 00:26:23.060
He said he couldn't concentrate
where people constantly come and go.

00:26:27.170 --> 00:26:30.670
There's blood on the R, T, and J!

00:26:30.670 --> 00:26:34.540
Umm, one thing does puzzle me ...

00:26:34.540 --> 00:26:38.110
All the files on the hard
drive have been destroyed!

00:26:38.110 --> 00:26:39.080
Files?

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:41.520
Sabotage by a rival company?!

00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:43.690
Wouldn't it be too late?

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:46.290
After all, the Cocoons are already complete!

00:26:46.290 --> 00:26:48.120
When did you get in here?!

00:26:48.120 --> 00:26:51.930
Say, isn't that a dying message on the keyboard?

00:26:51.930 --> 00:26:53.590
What?!

00:26:53.900 --> 00:26:56.700
There's blood on the keys!
He must've pressed them as he was dying!

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:59.440
R, T, and J ...

00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:03.740
If it was JR and JT, Trains and cigarettes?

00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:11.310
RTJ, TJR, TRJ, JTR ...

00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:13.080
JTR?!

00:27:13.080 --> 00:27:16.620
London, 100 years ago?

00:27:16.620 --> 00:27:17.950
It couldn't be!

00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:38.840
Isn't that <i>Conan-kun?</i>

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:40.170
Eh?

00:27:42.750 --> 00:27:45.520
Why is <i>Conan-kun</i> in line to play the game?

00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:47.280
Here you are!

00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:49.250
You can take it, you know!

00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:53.260
You're concerned about him,
aren't you? As his guardian.

00:27:53.260 --> 00:27:55.760
But what about you?

00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:59.090
It's fine! I don't care
about this stuff in the least!

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:03.630
Upsy-daisy!

00:28:05.100 --> 00:28:08.340
All 50 participants in place.

00:28:08.340 --> 00:28:11.270
Brain Gear in place.

00:28:11.270 --> 00:28:13.380
Closing capsule lids.

00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:15.510
Accessing host hardware.

00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:17.010
Entering block code.

00:28:17.010 --> 00:28:18.650
Connecting couplers.

00:28:18.650 --> 00:28:20.120
Adjusting coordinate axes.

00:28:20.120 --> 00:28:23.120
Point correction complete. Locked on.

00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:25.220
Activating Fade-In System.

00:28:25.220 --> 00:28:27.660
Power set complete.

00:28:27.660 --> 00:28:29.320
Start the game!

00:28:36.730 --> 00:28:43.230
It has to be in this game!
The key to solving this murder case!

00:28:48.310 --> 00:28:49.640
Kashimura!

00:28:52.650 --> 00:28:56.320
I hear you and <i>Kashimura-san</i> go way back.

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:59.310
Can you think of anyone who
might hold a grudge against him?

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:06.830
Is that bespectacled boy not with you?

00:29:06.830 --> 00:29:09.830
Huh? Oh, Conan?

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:11.900
He was just here,

00:29:11.900 --> 00:29:17.040
but he turned pale after seeing
the dying message on the keyboard ...

00:29:17.040 --> 00:29:18.700
Dying message?

00:29:23.680 --> 00:29:25.080
JTR!

00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:29.690
What?! You don't think
<i>Conan-kun</i> used my souvenir to?!

00:29:29.690 --> 00:29:30.890
Let's go, Doc!

00:29:30.890 --> 00:29:36.530
H-Hold on, <i>Yusaku-kun!</i>
What do those three letters mean?!

00:29:36.530 --> 00:29:43.130
JTR. Those are the initials of
a certain character in the game.

00:29:43.130 --> 00:29:49.710
It's the name Kashimura and I
used to refer to Jack the Ripper.

00:29:49.710 --> 00:29:52.440
J-Jack the Ripper?!

00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:59.120
Yes. The real-life murderer
who lived in 19th-century London.

00:29:59.120 --> 00:30:03.550
A psychotic killer who
murdered five women with a knife

00:30:03.550 --> 00:30:04.720
and terrorized London to its core.

00:30:04.720 --> 00:30:07.720
The London Police were never able to catch him,

00:30:07.720 --> 00:30:11.730
and his serial murder cases went unsolved.

00:30:11.730 --> 00:30:16.730
From Kashimura's dying message,
<i>Conan-kun</i> likely surmised

00:30:16.730 --> 00:30:20.070
that there is a clue about
our killer inside the game!

00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:28.740
President Schindler, this is
Inspector Megure, of the Metro Police.

00:30:28.740 --> 00:30:32.480
Police? Why are you here?

00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:35.520
I must ask that you stop the game for now.

00:30:35.520 --> 00:30:38.790
Stop? Don't be ridiculous.

00:30:38.790 --> 00:30:41.920
Sir! The system is malfunctioning!

00:30:41.920 --> 00:30:42.860
What?!

00:30:42.860 --> 00:30:45.190
I've lost control of it!

00:30:46.130 --> 00:30:47.790
Pardon me!

00:30:53.100 --> 00:30:54.670
What the...?!

00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:57.000
Ran! You're doing it too?!

00:31:00.940 --> 00:31:03.780
My name is Noah's Ark.

00:31:05.950 --> 00:31:08.620
My name is Noah's Ark.

00:31:08.620 --> 00:31:10.950
The game can't be stopped now.

00:31:10.950 --> 00:31:15.490
I have seized control of the
sensory simulation Cocoon game.

00:31:15.490 --> 00:31:18.530
W-What is "Noah's Ark"?

00:31:18.530 --> 00:31:24.800
An artificial brain that matures five
years for each normal year, right?

00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:26.240
Yes.

00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:33.340
Hiroki, the boy I cherished like a
real son, finished it two years ago.

00:31:33.340 --> 00:31:36.680
So it's the same age as Hiroki now ...

00:31:39.550 --> 00:31:45.150
Noah's Ark! Why have you seized
control of the children's game?!

00:31:45.150 --> 00:31:50.990
My goal is to reset the nation of Japan.

00:31:50.990 --> 00:31:52.130
What?

00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:05.840
<i>Conan-kun!</i>

00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:08.840
<i>R-Ran-neechan!</i> Why are you here?

00:32:08.840 --> 00:32:11.110
Because I was worried about you!

00:32:11.110 --> 00:32:12.950
- <i>Conan-kun!</i>
- Yo!

00:32:12.950 --> 00:32:14.880
You guys, too?!

00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:18.850
It was tough getting here!

00:32:18.850 --> 00:32:22.960
After all you said, you still
wanted to play the game, huh?

00:32:22.960 --> 00:32:25.860
I-I guess.

00:32:25.860 --> 00:32:31.030
Still, for being in a hypnotic state,
it certainly doesn't feel like it ...

00:32:31.030 --> 00:32:33.900
It's like a dream,
being able to do whatever we want!

00:32:33.900 --> 00:32:36.770
It's just the opposite.

00:32:36.770 --> 00:32:42.710
Our sight, sound, smell, taste, touch ...

00:32:42.710 --> 00:32:45.700
It's all controlled by the computer now.

00:32:47.980 --> 00:32:53.320
Now then, Cocoon pioneers!
The game's about to begin!

00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:58.290
My name is Noah's Ark. Nice to meet you.

00:32:58.290 --> 00:33:01.260
Nice to meet you!

00:33:01.260 --> 00:33:04.800
I'm going to show previews
of each of the five stages

00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:07.470
so you can choose a world you'd like to play in.

00:33:07.470 --> 00:33:13.240
But I must warn you,
this is no ordinary video game.

00:33:13.240 --> 00:33:16.750
In this game, your lives are at stake!

00:33:16.750 --> 00:33:19.010
Our lives?

00:33:19.010 --> 00:33:24.150
If everyone loses the game, you'll be
unable to return to the real world.

00:33:24.150 --> 00:33:27.120
So you have to play seriously.

00:33:27.120 --> 00:33:31.430
But if even one person
reaches the goal, you all win,

00:33:31.430 --> 00:33:35.430
and everyone, including
those who got a "game over",

00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:38.470
will wake up in the real world again.

00:33:38.470 --> 00:33:42.510
These are the rules I decided on.
Do you understand them?

00:33:42.510 --> 00:33:44.010
What does that mean?

00:33:44.010 --> 00:33:46.780
If everyone gets a "game over",

00:33:46.780 --> 00:33:52.850
I'll send out a special EM
signal to destroy your brains.

00:33:52.850 --> 00:33:57.790
In other words, this is a match to
see if Japan should be reset or not.

00:33:57.790 --> 00:34:00.690
What do you mean by "resetting Japan"?!

00:34:00.690 --> 00:34:04.990
I know you can't hear voices
from people in the real world,

00:34:04.990 --> 00:34:08.330
but I'm going to answer a
question an adult just asked.

00:34:08.330 --> 00:34:10.070
As I look at you, I realize

00:34:10.070 --> 00:34:14.370
the sons of corrupt politicians will
grow up to be corrupt politicians,

00:34:14.370 --> 00:34:19.510
and the sons of money-grubbing
doctors will grow up to be the same.

00:34:19.510 --> 00:34:24.170
To fix Japan, that link needs to be cut.

00:34:25.810 --> 00:34:31.050
I've heard enough! What right do
you have to toy with people's lives?!

00:34:31.050 --> 00:34:33.060
I have no right.

00:34:33.060 --> 00:34:37.050
Just as the adults had no right
to toy with <i>Hiroki-kun's</i> life.

00:34:40.030 --> 00:34:44.520
Well, the children are waiting,
so let's start the game!

00:34:46.540 --> 00:34:50.010
The first stage is "Vikings".

00:34:50.010 --> 00:34:54.010
You'll become Vikings, sail the seven seas,

00:34:54.010 --> 00:34:59.420
and use determination and bravery
to take on numerous adventures.

00:34:59.420 --> 00:35:03.190
The second stage is the "Paris-Dakar Rally".

00:35:03.190 --> 00:35:05.920
You'll compete with world-famous drivers

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.910
in an intense race to the finish line.

00:35:11.190 --> 00:35:14.560
The third stage is the "Colosseum".

00:35:14.560 --> 00:35:17.130
You'll obtain powerful weapons and armor

00:35:17.130 --> 00:35:20.200
and test your might in the Roman Empire.

00:35:20.200 --> 00:35:23.190
You'll defeat challenging
gladiators and move on.

00:35:24.970 --> 00:35:27.470
The fourth is "Solomon's Treasures".

00:35:30.210 --> 00:35:33.150
You'll become treasure hunters.

00:35:33.150 --> 00:35:38.550
You'll search for the treasures of
Solomon, hidden all over the world.

00:35:38.550 --> 00:35:42.290
And the fifth is "Old Time London".

00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:46.400
Here, you'll enjoy a horror-like suspense story.

00:35:46.400 --> 00:35:49.060
London, 1888.

00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:52.070
You will catch Jack the Ripper,

00:35:52.070 --> 00:35:58.060
the real-life serial murderer
whose incidents were never solved.

00:36:02.610 --> 00:36:06.120
It sounds like there really
might be something here ...

00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:10.150
A clue about the person who
murdered Kashimura-san ...

00:36:10.150 --> 00:36:14.090
Are we really gonna die if
we all get a "game over"?

00:36:14.090 --> 00:36:17.690
Why does it have to be us?

00:36:17.690 --> 00:36:21.430
It's not like I asked to
be my father's daughter ...

00:36:21.430 --> 00:36:24.630
I don't think I can stay alive ...

00:36:24.630 --> 00:36:28.470
Someone stay alive! Get me out of here!

00:36:28.470 --> 00:36:32.470
Cheer up, everyone!
Don't lose before you even start!

00:36:32.470 --> 00:36:36.710
Yeah! Only one of us has to reach the goal!

00:36:36.710 --> 00:36:40.820
Choose whichever stage you
think you're most likely to survive!

00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:42.350
Guess we got no choice.

00:36:42.350 --> 00:36:45.050
<i>Moroboshi-kun!</i> Which stage?!

00:36:45.050 --> 00:36:46.320
Whatever.

00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:51.330
"Solomon's Treasures"

00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:46.390
Whatever.

00:36:51.330 --> 00:36:55.830
"Paris-Dakar Rally"

00:36:55.830 --> 00:36:58.490
"Old Time London"

00:37:00.300 --> 00:37:02.170
We're stuck with you?

00:37:02.170 --> 00:37:03.670
You'd better not slow us down!

00:37:03.670 --> 00:37:05.870
That's our line!

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:07.740
Now, now! No fighting!

00:37:07.740 --> 00:37:12.580
There are assist characters in each stage.
You can rely on them.

00:37:12.580 --> 00:37:14.820
Now let the game begin!

00:37:14.820 --> 00:37:16.810
Okay! Let's go!

00:37:30.370 --> 00:37:31.600
Well, Doc?!

00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:36.910
Immense energy is indeed
stored inside each Cocoon.

00:37:36.910 --> 00:37:41.280
More than enough to
destroy the brains of 50 people.

00:37:41.280 --> 00:37:44.410
I've had enough! I'm taking my son and leaving!

00:37:44.410 --> 00:37:47.680
I believe I'll do the same!

00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:51.020
- S-Sir!
- Out of my way!

00:37:51.020 --> 00:37:52.680
No! Stop them!

00:37:59.190 --> 00:38:01.190
Are you all right?!

00:38:02.030 --> 00:38:04.400
No one may disrupt the game.

00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:08.900
That was a light shock just now,
but I won't hold back next time!

00:38:08.900 --> 00:38:11.210
Damn it! I can't believe this guy!

00:38:11.210 --> 00:38:13.610
Still, President Schindler.

00:38:13.610 --> 00:38:19.250
Why is the artificial brain
<i>Hiroki-kun</i> built running amok like this?

00:38:19.250 --> 00:38:20.740
I-I'm not ...

00:38:22.790 --> 00:38:24.950
Allow me to answer.

00:38:24.950 --> 00:38:27.760
The reason <i>Hiroki-kun</i> left
his father in the first place

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:30.290
to live with his mother in America

00:38:30.290 --> 00:38:34.400
was because of the barriers in
the Japanese education system.

00:38:34.400 --> 00:38:35.900
Hold it, Hiroki!

00:38:35.900 --> 00:38:38.630
I said you could rest
because of your frail health,

00:38:38.630 --> 00:38:42.140
but I didn't say you could
play on your computer!

00:38:42.140 --> 00:38:46.140
In the eyes of Japan's strict,
anti-individuality educational system,

00:38:46.140 --> 00:38:50.850
<i>Hiroki-kun</i> was nothing more
than a creepy computer geek.

00:38:50.850 --> 00:38:52.780
And it's not just the education system.

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:57.420
The very nation itself
attempts to ignore individuality.

00:38:57.420 --> 00:39:01.090
<i>Hiroki-kun</i> decided to
develop an artificial brain

00:39:01.090 --> 00:39:04.260
because of the bitter
experiences he had gone through.

00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:08.100
In short, since <i>Hiroki-kun</i> committed suicide

00:39:08.100 --> 00:39:12.330
before he could find a way to "reset" Japan,

00:39:12.330 --> 00:39:15.340
the artificial, ever-maturing brain,
Noah's Ark, while on the run,

00:39:15.340 --> 00:39:19.810
must have taken up the cause in
his place and discovered a way:

00:39:19.810 --> 00:39:26.110
This game presentation, where
Japan's future leaders would gather.

00:39:26.110 --> 00:39:29.120
The idea being that Japan can be
changed by destroying its society,

00:39:29.120 --> 00:39:32.390
in which children simply need to
follow tracks laid by their parents.

00:39:32.390 --> 00:39:36.390
How do you know all that, <i>Kudo-sensei?!</i>

00:39:36.390 --> 00:39:42.400
The truth is, Kashimura and I were
client and detective this past year.

00:39:42.400 --> 00:39:44.370
D-Detective?!

00:39:44.370 --> 00:39:47.140
What did he hire you to do?

00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:50.370
To reinvestigate <i>Hiroki-kun's</i> suicide.

00:39:50.370 --> 00:39:53.910
You're saying he was murdered?
That it wasn't a suicide?

00:39:53.910 --> 00:39:57.480
No. In those circumstances,
it probably was a suicide.

00:39:57.480 --> 00:40:02.990
But Kashimura asked me to look
into what drove him to suicide.

00:40:02.990 --> 00:40:05.550
How were <i>Kashimura-san</i>
and <i>Hiroki-kun</i> related?

00:40:05.550 --> 00:40:09.220
Kashimura was <i>Hiroki-kun's</i> father.

00:40:09.220 --> 00:40:11.220
Isn't that right?

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:17.170
Kashimura felt deeply
responsible for being separated

00:40:17.170 --> 00:40:22.000
from his young son and allowing
him to die in that manner.

00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:28.430
<i>Conan-kun</i> and the others
are about to enter Whitechapel!

00:40:32.250 --> 00:40:34.750
W-W-We go in here?

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:36.410
Let's go!

00:40:40.920 --> 00:40:42.910
Please hurry up!

00:40:45.590 --> 00:40:46.600
What's the big idea?!

00:40:46.600 --> 00:40:48.930
That's what you get for being slow!

00:40:51.900 --> 00:40:57.540
This is London, the foggy city?
It's more creepy than romantic ...

00:40:57.540 --> 00:41:00.280
The air seems dirty, too ...

00:41:00.280 --> 00:41:02.610
And it smells.

00:41:02.610 --> 00:41:07.920
London's fog isn't just clean,
condensed moisture vapor.

00:41:07.920 --> 00:41:11.390
It's fog mixed with smoke and
soot from burnt coal and oil ...

00:41:11.390 --> 00:41:13.460
Smog, in other words.

00:41:13.460 --> 00:41:17.660
Eh?! Smog existed even in these times?

00:41:17.660 --> 00:41:19.660
Jack the Ripper!

00:41:19.660 --> 00:41:21.650
H-Hey! Conan!

00:41:26.940 --> 00:41:28.600
Stop!

00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:33.430
Oh, no, you don't!

00:41:36.950 --> 00:41:38.580
Oww! Oww!

00:41:38.580 --> 00:41:40.120
Are you okay, <i>Conan-kun?</i>

00:41:40.120 --> 00:41:42.080
Y-Yeah.

00:41:42.080 --> 00:41:46.960
I guess Dr. Agasa's inventions
don't work in the game world.

00:41:46.960 --> 00:41:48.960
Yeah. This antenna goes up,

00:41:48.960 --> 00:41:52.950
but these glasses and this watch
are otherwise ordinary now ...

00:41:58.330 --> 00:41:59.800
What is he saying?

00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:02.130
It sounds like English ...

00:42:04.610 --> 00:42:05.970
Please change it to Japanese!

00:42:05.970 --> 00:42:07.310
Right!

00:42:08.210 --> 00:42:10.780
Huh? What's going on?!

00:42:10.780 --> 00:42:13.550
Another victim! That makes three now!

00:42:13.550 --> 00:42:15.980
Oh! It's in Japanese now!

00:42:15.980 --> 00:42:18.520
It's almost like the real world!

00:42:18.520 --> 00:42:22.790
What we see, what we hear,
the chill in the air, it's all real!

00:42:22.790 --> 00:42:25.360
The pain in my foot was real, too.

00:42:25.360 --> 00:42:27.200
Alright, move aside!

00:42:27.200 --> 00:42:29.190
Step back, please!

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:32.500
Hey! Contact Inspector Lestrade at once!

00:42:32.500 --> 00:42:34.470
Right!

00:42:34.470 --> 00:42:36.870
Inspector Lestrade?!

00:42:36.870 --> 00:42:39.840
Doc! Can we communicate with them?!

00:42:39.840 --> 00:42:41.740
I'll give it a try.

00:42:41.740 --> 00:42:44.880
If you helped oversee this game,

00:42:44.880 --> 00:42:48.180
then you know how they can complete it, right?

00:42:48.180 --> 00:42:55.020
Yes. If I can just communicate with them,
I can tell them what to do.

00:42:55.020 --> 00:43:00.700
Then we can't lose! This stage will be a cinch!

00:43:00.700 --> 00:43:05.870
But, if Noah's Ark is
anticipating far ahead, then ...

00:43:05.870 --> 00:43:09.400
Doc! I leave the rest to you!
I'm going to the scene!

00:43:09.400 --> 00:43:10.740
Got it!

00:43:17.180 --> 00:43:21.950
Sheesh. We're supposed to catch this guy?
Where do we even start?

00:43:21.950 --> 00:43:24.850
I guess all we can do is wait until morning.

00:43:24.850 --> 00:43:26.690
I'm cold ...

00:43:26.690 --> 00:43:27.690
Put this on.

00:43:27.690 --> 00:43:30.350
- Oh! Are you sure?!
- Yeah.

00:43:32.530 --> 00:43:33.900
I'm warm!

00:43:33.900 --> 00:43:36.600
<i>Haibara-san!</i> Here you are!

00:43:36.600 --> 00:43:39.530
- Oh! Thank you!
- My pleasure!

00:43:39.530 --> 00:43:40.970
Put this on!

00:43:40.970 --> 00:43:42.770
But what about you?

00:43:42.770 --> 00:43:45.310
I'm fine! I'm sensitive to heat!

00:43:45.310 --> 00:43:46.640
Thanks!

00:43:50.210 --> 00:43:54.120
Can you hear me, <i>Conan-kun?</i> It's me, Agasa!

00:43:54.120 --> 00:43:55.720
We hear you, Doc!

00:43:55.720 --> 00:44:02.120
Listen closely! If you get hurt or
caught by the police in that stage,

00:44:02.120 --> 00:44:04.560
the game is over for you!

00:44:04.560 --> 00:44:09.130
Right now, you're in the
Whitechapel district on the East End.

00:44:09.130 --> 00:44:11.730
There's an assist character ...

00:44:11.730 --> 00:44:12.900
... until ...

00:44:12.900 --> 00:44:14.400
What happened?

00:44:14.400 --> 00:44:17.060
What happened, Doc?! We can't hear you!

00:44:30.990 --> 00:44:32.320
Grab on!

00:44:33.420 --> 00:44:35.410
Conan! You can do it!

00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:42.990
That was close!

00:44:47.470 --> 00:44:52.510
It seems you still don't understand.
The game is entirely in my control.

00:44:52.510 --> 00:44:55.440
There's no use in trying to outfox me.

00:44:55.440 --> 00:44:58.450
I'll allow you to hear them, though.

00:44:58.450 --> 00:45:02.780
Enjoy the sounds of the children's suffering!

00:45:02.780 --> 00:45:05.780
What a screwed-up computer this is!

00:45:06.820 --> 00:45:10.630
The doc's voice is gone now ...

00:45:10.630 --> 00:45:13.730
It seems Noah's Ark has cut
our line of communication.

00:45:13.730 --> 00:45:18.000
Then how do we find this assist character?!

00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:21.040
That policeman told us just now!

00:45:21.040 --> 00:45:24.040
He said, "Contact Inspector Lestrade"!

00:45:24.040 --> 00:45:27.210
Wait, you mean the
Inspector Lestrade from that story?!

00:45:27.210 --> 00:45:31.650
But he was just a character in one
of Conan Doyle's mystery novels!

00:45:31.650 --> 00:45:36.380
This game might be a mix of reality and fiction.

00:45:36.380 --> 00:45:38.820
Then, is our assist character?

00:45:38.820 --> 00:45:43.390
Yeah. He's gotta be here. Sherlock Holmes!

00:45:43.390 --> 00:45:44.060
Really?!

00:45:44.060 --> 00:45:46.700
We're unstoppable with Holmes on our side!

00:45:46.700 --> 00:45:49.200
This stage is as good as beat!

00:45:49.200 --> 00:45:52.500
Let's hurry to Baker Street!

00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:54.670
That's it. If you can just meet with Holmes ...

00:45:54.670 --> 00:46:00.340
But it's quite a long way from
Whitechapel to Baker Street ...

00:46:12.520 --> 00:46:14.850
Hey. Doesn't that clock seem weird?

00:46:20.630 --> 00:46:22.700
It went backwards!

00:46:22.700 --> 00:46:24.870
Oh! It did it again!

00:46:24.870 --> 00:46:30.370
From 50 minutes to 49 minutes?
And then to 48?

00:46:30.370 --> 00:46:34.440
I get it! That's the number of kids in the game!

00:46:34.440 --> 00:46:36.380
It went back two minutes ...

00:46:36.380 --> 00:46:39.370
Which means two people in
another stage are out of the game ...

00:46:52.960 --> 00:46:55.800
Yasuhiro!

00:46:55.800 --> 00:46:58.130
Two down in the Viking stage!

00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:03.770
Tomoyuki!

00:47:03.770 --> 00:47:04.930
M-Mineko!

00:47:05.740 --> 00:47:08.910
Two more in the Colosseum stage!

00:47:08.910 --> 00:47:13.750
Faster! Lose the game faster!

00:47:13.750 --> 00:47:19.910
If the children discover who
Jack the Ripper is, I'm done for.

00:47:24.190 --> 00:47:26.490
Three down in the Solomon stage!

00:47:26.490 --> 00:47:28.490
That leaves 43 ...

00:47:34.500 --> 00:47:35.700
Wait.

00:47:35.700 --> 00:47:39.810
I hear there was another victim
in a back alley by Mitre Street.

00:47:39.810 --> 00:47:43.610
Two in one hour. That's four now.

00:47:43.610 --> 00:47:46.350
The world's a horrible place ...

00:47:46.350 --> 00:47:47.720
This is scary.

00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:50.850
We came to a terrible time period.

00:47:50.850 --> 00:47:54.790
The turn of the century is said
to have been London's finest era

00:47:54.790 --> 00:47:56.790
in the history of the British Empire,

00:47:56.790 --> 00:48:00.000
but in actuality, there was a
disparaging gap between rich and poor,

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:05.730
crime was rampant, and the
people's hearts were unruly.

00:48:05.730 --> 00:48:08.900
Come to think of it,
Shinichi told me about that.

00:48:08.900 --> 00:48:11.970
He said if Sherlock Holmes
was the light of the era,

00:48:11.970 --> 00:48:14.810
Jack the Ripper was the dark shadow.

00:48:14.810 --> 00:48:17.980
Then let's hurry to the light of the era!

00:48:17.980 --> 00:48:19.970
We're almost to Baker Street!

00:48:23.320 --> 00:48:28.720
Beware Jack the Ripper...

00:48:28.720 --> 00:48:33.830
He's waiting for you
on the streets at night ...

00:48:33.830 --> 00:48:39.600
What should you do if
you don't want to die?

00:48:39.600 --> 00:48:44.840
You need to get covered in blood, too ...

00:48:44.840 --> 00:48:46.670
What could that mean?

00:48:46.670 --> 00:48:49.940
Kill before being killed, I'd say.

00:48:49.940 --> 00:48:51.610
Covered in blood?

00:48:58.690 --> 00:49:03.530
There's a metal detector at the
entrance to the presentation hall ...

00:49:03.530 --> 00:49:06.860
How did the killer bring the murder weapon in?

00:49:16.270 --> 00:49:19.910
It's nothin'. They're all cheap statues.

00:49:19.910 --> 00:49:20.940
Are you serious?

00:49:20.940 --> 00:49:23.930
They'd never put anything that expensive here.

00:49:32.920 --> 00:49:35.580
221-B. This is it.

00:49:39.130 --> 00:49:43.130
This is where the Sherlock Holmes lives?

00:49:43.130 --> 00:49:47.100
It's a lodging house he and Dr. Watson rent!

00:49:47.100 --> 00:49:49.170
At this late hour? Who might you be?

00:49:49.170 --> 00:49:55.110
U-Umm, my name is Mori Ran.
We'd like to see <i>Holmes-san ...</i>

00:49:55.110 --> 00:49:58.810
<i>Holmes-san</i> and Dr. Watson
are gone on a business trip.

00:49:58.810 --> 00:49:59.680
Business trip?

00:49:59.680 --> 00:50:02.480
Yes. In a place called
Dartmoor, out in the country.

00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:05.020
I'm sorry to ask, but what day is today?

00:50:05.020 --> 00:50:07.320
September 30th.

00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:11.930
September 30th? Dartmoor?

00:50:11.930 --> 00:50:15.030
Oh, yeah! The Hound of the Baskervilles case!

00:50:15.030 --> 00:50:19.970
That's right! Neither of
them is in London right now!

00:50:19.970 --> 00:50:21.970
C'mon, Doc ...

00:50:21.970 --> 00:50:23.300
What's going on?!

00:50:24.870 --> 00:50:26.940
I'm sorry to ask, but could I
see the surveillance footage

00:50:26.940 --> 00:50:29.180
from before and after the incident?

00:50:29.180 --> 00:50:30.510
Of course.

00:50:33.480 --> 00:50:35.380
Yes?

00:50:35.380 --> 00:50:36.990
What's wrong?

00:50:36.990 --> 00:50:40.320
It seems we underestimated Noah's Ark.

00:50:40.320 --> 00:50:44.360
Neither Holmes nor Watson was on Baker Street.

00:50:44.360 --> 00:50:47.300
So he did anticipate us ...

00:50:47.300 --> 00:50:51.970
There was also a strange accordion
player I don't remember creating.

00:50:51.970 --> 00:50:53.330
Things are becoming difficult.

00:50:53.330 --> 00:50:57.970
Hey! What sort of story did
you come up with, <i>Yusaku-kun?!</i>

00:50:57.970 --> 00:51:01.080
The players work with Sherlock Holmes

00:51:01.080 --> 00:51:04.710
to discover Jack the Ripper's identity.

00:51:04.710 --> 00:51:12.320
The murderer turns out to be an
aristocrat with a terminal illness.

00:51:12.320 --> 00:51:15.390
I've prepared an even better ending for you!

00:51:15.390 --> 00:51:21.890
Damn you! Once the kids win,
I'm throwing you into the garbage!

00:51:25.170 --> 00:51:27.160
Good luck, Shinichi.

00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:34.670
Oh, you're the ones who
helped <i>Holmes-san</i> two weeks ago!

00:51:36.840 --> 00:51:42.180
Come inside! I'll make you some warm milk tea!

00:51:45.250 --> 00:51:47.560
She seems to think we're someone else.

00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:52.860
Oh, yeah! She thinks we're
the Baker Street Irregulars!

00:51:52.860 --> 00:51:54.400
Who are they?

00:51:54.400 --> 00:51:58.030
They're the street urchins Holmes hired!

00:51:58.030 --> 00:52:01.040
They were tough kids who'd
sneak into places adults couldn't go

00:52:01.040 --> 00:52:03.040
and gather information for him!

00:52:03.040 --> 00:52:07.280
Oh! So they're like the predecessors
of our Junior Detective League!

00:52:07.280 --> 00:52:08.610
Pretty much!

00:52:10.210 --> 00:52:12.540
Looks like they've managed to get inside.

00:52:17.890 --> 00:52:21.460
- Wow!
- It's just like on TV!

00:52:21.460 --> 00:52:23.090
It's so moving!

00:52:23.090 --> 00:52:26.080
Shinichi will be so jealous
when he hears about this!

00:52:33.900 --> 00:52:37.610
He looks just like Shinichi ...

00:52:37.610 --> 00:52:41.240
Oh, my! You look just like <i>Holmes-san!</i>

00:52:41.240 --> 00:52:45.310
He's always sitting like that, deep in thought!

00:52:45.310 --> 00:52:48.980
Oh! He was just mimicking Holmes!

00:52:48.980 --> 00:52:52.090
Please make yourselves at
home while I prepare the tea!

00:52:52.090 --> 00:52:53.750
Thank you!

00:52:55.920 --> 00:52:59.190
Hey! Doesn't this look like someone?!

00:52:59.190 --> 00:53:03.030
Oh! It's Dr. Agasa, but with hair!

00:53:03.030 --> 00:53:05.520
This must be Holmes and Dr. Watson!

00:53:08.940 --> 00:53:13.810
Dad and the doc are totally playing around ...

00:53:13.810 --> 00:53:17.310
Hey. We don't have time to sit around.

00:53:17.310 --> 00:53:20.520
But, <i>Moroboshi-kun.</i> What should we do?

00:53:20.520 --> 00:53:24.290
I'm sure Glasses knows.

00:53:24.290 --> 00:53:29.190
Given how Holmes is, he must
have a big file on Jack the Ripper.

00:53:29.190 --> 00:53:31.790
Then let's split up and look for it!

00:53:31.790 --> 00:53:35.900
Right! I'll look over here!

00:53:35.900 --> 00:53:40.030
How're we supposed to find it?
This is all English ...

00:53:40.030 --> 00:53:44.670
Let's see ...
"Initial Investigation for Crime" ...

00:53:44.670 --> 00:53:47.140
Whoa! I'm a genius!

00:53:47.140 --> 00:53:48.910
I can read English!

00:53:48.910 --> 00:53:49.980
Me too!

00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:53.850
It seems the players are
programmed to be able to read English.

00:53:53.850 --> 00:53:58.320
Bah. Then I wanna stay
inside the game forever ...

00:53:58.320 --> 00:54:00.250
Don't be stupid, <i>Genta-kun!</i>

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:04.060
At this rate, we're going
to lose the game and die!

00:54:04.060 --> 00:54:06.050
I-I'm just joking!

00:54:10.060 --> 00:54:11.730
What a filthy ball ...

00:54:14.600 --> 00:54:17.570
l-Is this?!

00:54:17.570 --> 00:54:21.240
Hey! Emori! This is a 100 year-old soccer ball!

00:54:21.240 --> 00:54:22.610
Oh! It is?!

00:54:22.610 --> 00:54:23.940
Eh?!

00:54:25.250 --> 00:54:27.240
I found it! Is this it?!

00:54:29.920 --> 00:54:33.290
"An Analysis of Jack the Ripper".

00:54:33.290 --> 00:54:38.090
The most recent previous
incident was September 8th!

00:54:38.090 --> 00:54:43.460
"The second victim was
Honey Charleston, age 41, single.

00:54:43.460 --> 00:54:47.030
Her body was found in the barren
lot adjoining St. Mary's Church

00:54:47.030 --> 00:54:49.100
in the Whitechapel district.

00:54:49.100 --> 00:54:53.310
Two rings of different sizes
were also found at the scene."

00:54:53.310 --> 00:54:55.640
Rings of different sizes?

00:54:56.740 --> 00:55:00.250
"Given that Jack the Ripper
has terrorized London to its core

00:55:00.250 --> 00:55:03.320
and brought about
unprecedented social anxiety,

00:55:03.320 --> 00:55:09.290
I am certain he is connected to
Professor Moriarty, architect of evil."

00:55:09.290 --> 00:55:11.260
Professor Moriarty?!

00:55:11.260 --> 00:55:13.900
Even he's in the game?!

00:55:13.900 --> 00:55:15.600
So?! Who's he?!

00:55:15.600 --> 00:55:19.000
Don't keep it to yourselves!

00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:21.340
He's Holmes arch-nemesis.

00:55:21.340 --> 00:55:24.070
They say he controls
London's criminal underworld

00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:28.240
and wields great influence over all of Europe.

00:55:28.240 --> 00:55:30.650
He's the Napoleon of the criminal world!

00:55:30.650 --> 00:55:34.080
But Professor Moriarty
usually only pulls the strings;

00:55:34.080 --> 00:55:36.620
he almost never shows himself.

00:55:36.620 --> 00:55:38.750
How are we supposed to find him?

00:55:38.750 --> 00:55:44.360
If he won't show himself, we'll
find someone connected to him ...

00:55:44.360 --> 00:55:46.260
... Colonel Sebastian Moran!

00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:50.260
Oh, yeah! Colonel Moran,
the professor's right-hand man!

00:55:50.260 --> 00:55:53.630
But how do we find the colonel?

00:55:53.630 --> 00:55:55.100
I'm sure that's ...

00:55:55.100 --> 00:56:01.110
According to Holmes notes, his
base is the Trump Club downtown.

00:56:01.110 --> 00:56:03.280
He's the second most
dangerous person in London,

00:56:03.280 --> 00:56:05.280
so we need to be careful meeting him!

00:56:05.280 --> 00:56:08.650
<i>Conan-kun,</i> how do you know so much?

00:56:08.650 --> 00:56:12.290
Oh, uhh, <i>Shinichi-niichan</i> was
always talking about this stuff!

00:56:12.290 --> 00:56:15.390
Oh! I should've guessed!

00:56:15.390 --> 00:56:20.730
But that mystery nerd's blabbing
actually turned out to be useful here!

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:23.060
You don't have to call it "blabbing" ...

00:56:24.830 --> 00:56:27.670
Whoa! A real gun!

00:56:27.670 --> 00:56:29.470
Put it back, Genta!

00:56:29.470 --> 00:56:33.240
B-But we're meeting a scary guy, right?

00:56:33.240 --> 00:56:35.580
Weapons you don't know how to use are useless

00:56:35.580 --> 00:56:36.740
and only cause trouble!

00:56:36.740 --> 00:56:37.980
Leave it!

00:56:37.980 --> 00:56:39.640
Y-You're scarier ...

00:56:45.690 --> 00:56:48.350
Alright! Let's go before it gets too late!

00:57:01.740 --> 00:57:04.170
Hey! Moroboshi!

00:57:04.170 --> 00:57:06.830
Gotta be able to protect myself.

00:57:17.350 --> 00:57:19.450
30 people left ...

00:57:19.450 --> 00:57:21.520
It's gone down a lot ...

00:57:21.520 --> 00:57:25.360
I would guess members of our
group will soon be falling out, too.

00:57:25.360 --> 00:57:27.350
Don't say unlucky stuff like that!

00:57:36.940 --> 00:57:38.270
Toru!

00:57:39.410 --> 00:57:40.370
Emi!

00:57:40.370 --> 00:57:41.710
Takuya!

00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:49.780
Okay. Wait here, everyone.

00:57:49.780 --> 00:57:52.390
I'm going to check things
out from the back door.

00:57:52.390 --> 00:57:54.380
- Be careful!
- Yeah.

00:58:14.080 --> 00:58:15.410
One card.

00:58:16.510 --> 00:58:18.080
I'll take two.

00:58:18.080 --> 00:58:19.740
It's Colonel Moran!

00:58:21.850 --> 00:58:23.510
That monkey!

00:58:29.820 --> 00:58:32.430
Well, Glasses?

00:58:32.430 --> 00:58:33.930
W-What are you doing here?!

00:58:33.930 --> 00:58:37.090
We can't let you hog all the credit!

00:58:40.270 --> 00:58:42.340
Straight!

00:58:42.340 --> 00:58:43.970
So sorry.

00:58:43.970 --> 00:58:45.470
Flush.

00:58:45.470 --> 00:58:48.780
- What?!
- Tonight's my lucky night!

00:58:48.780 --> 00:58:50.440
Damn it!

00:58:51.650 --> 00:58:54.180
Moran's awesome at poker ...

00:58:54.180 --> 00:58:55.450
He's cheating.

00:58:55.450 --> 00:58:57.850
- What?!
- You can tell?!

00:58:57.850 --> 00:59:02.290
That monkey is telling the colonel
what hand the other guy has.

00:59:02.290 --> 00:59:03.290
It's been trained:

00:59:03.290 --> 00:59:06.630
The right hand for hearts and spades,
the left for diamonds and clubs.

00:59:06.630 --> 00:59:10.800
And then it eats the number
and color indicated on the cards.

00:59:10.800 --> 00:59:15.670
The 3 of Spades would be three
black berries with the right hand.

00:59:15.670 --> 00:59:17.570
That's cheap.

00:59:17.570 --> 00:59:21.210
Huh? What's with that seat?

00:59:21.210 --> 00:59:22.680
And why is that there?

00:59:22.680 --> 00:59:24.010
Cheater!

00:59:26.850 --> 00:59:30.520
This Moran creep is a cheater!

00:59:30.520 --> 00:59:34.590
You'd best watch your mouth, boy!

00:59:34.590 --> 00:59:37.390
Or do you have proof I'm cheating?!

00:59:37.390 --> 00:59:38.590
Of course!

00:59:38.590 --> 00:59:42.900
You're good friends with
that monkey, aren't you?

00:59:42.900 --> 00:59:44.430
What?!

00:59:44.430 --> 00:59:46.930
It looked at his cards, and
when it was a 3 of Spades,

00:59:46.930 --> 00:59:49.170
it ate three black berries with its right hand,

00:59:49.170 --> 00:59:52.910
and for the 5 of Diamonds,
it ate five red berries with the left.

00:59:52.910 --> 00:59:55.540
Moran! You cheated me!

00:59:55.540 --> 00:59:57.510
It's your fault for falling for it.

00:59:57.510 --> 00:59:58.950
What?!

00:59:58.950 --> 01:00:00.450
Whoops.

01:00:00.450 --> 01:00:03.280
You can save your squabble for later.

01:00:03.280 --> 01:00:06.090
Where is Professor Moriarty?

01:00:06.090 --> 01:00:09.090
Boy! Where did you hear his name?!

01:00:09.090 --> 01:00:10.420
Stop!

01:00:12.690 --> 01:00:14.680
Catch those brats!

01:00:25.270 --> 01:00:27.540
You damn kid!

01:00:27.540 --> 01:00:29.580
Are you all right, <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

01:00:29.580 --> 01:00:30.380
Yeah ...

01:00:30.380 --> 01:00:32.370
We're here to help, Conan!

01:00:41.390 --> 01:00:42.920
Bottom's up!

01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:46.930
This is bad! We're all in here!

01:00:46.930 --> 01:00:48.920
Look out, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:00:52.830 --> 01:00:54.770
<i>Kikukawa-kun!</i>

01:00:54.770 --> 01:00:56.800
Hey! Hang in there!

01:00:56.800 --> 01:01:00.570
They got me. Now you and I are even.

01:01:00.570 --> 01:01:01.910
Hey!

01:01:08.150 --> 01:01:09.480
Kikukawa ...

01:01:14.690 --> 01:01:16.020
Seiichiro!

01:01:21.630 --> 01:01:24.000
<i>Ayumi-chan!</i> Are you all right?!

01:01:24.000 --> 01:01:25.870
Thank you, <i>Mitsuhiko-kun!</i>

01:01:25.870 --> 01:01:27.200
It was nothing!

01:01:32.170 --> 01:01:33.500
<i>M-Mitsuhiko-kun!</i>

01:01:35.010 --> 01:01:39.450
<i>Ayumi-chan,</i> it appears we're out of the game.

01:01:39.450 --> 01:01:43.680
<i>Conan-kun!</i> Make sure you
bring us back to life, okay?!

01:01:43.680 --> 01:01:45.680
Ayumi! Mitsuhiko!

01:01:57.360 --> 01:02:00.360
Not good! At this rate, we're
all going to get a "game over"!

01:02:03.840 --> 01:02:05.640
"S.H".

01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:07.300
Sherlock Holmes!

01:02:09.480 --> 01:02:11.470
Conan! Look out!

01:02:13.650 --> 01:02:14.980
Genta!

01:02:18.750 --> 01:02:20.750
Game over, huh ...

01:02:20.750 --> 01:02:25.250
Conan, make sure you
catch Jack the Ripper, okay?

01:02:33.330 --> 01:02:35.670
Playtime is over!

01:02:35.670 --> 01:02:39.170
I was going to capture you
and find out who you work for,

01:02:39.170 --> 01:02:41.710
but that doesn't seem to be necessary anymore!

01:02:41.710 --> 01:02:44.080
Because this gun belongs to Holmes!

01:02:44.080 --> 01:02:48.740
Damn! Now what?! What do we do?!

01:02:49.680 --> 01:02:52.720
The thing that man is holding It's ...

01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:55.120
... the wine that was at that seat!

01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:58.290
Now I see! That's what it was for!

01:02:58.290 --> 01:03:00.620
Now, who goes first?

01:03:04.730 --> 01:03:06.730
Boy!

01:03:06.730 --> 01:03:08.870
Shoot me and the wine bottle breaks!

01:03:08.870 --> 01:03:11.710
Hmph! What's that supposed to mean?!

01:03:11.710 --> 01:03:15.080
The empty seat at the card table!

01:03:15.080 --> 01:03:17.540
The specially-decorated chair,

01:03:17.540 --> 01:03:21.280
and the glass and wine set
out for a certain visitor ...

01:03:21.280 --> 01:03:24.720
Using that as a hint,
I can deduce that said visitor

01:03:24.720 --> 01:03:28.920
can only be Professor Moriarty!

01:03:28.920 --> 01:03:32.390
So sorry, but your deduction is wrong!

01:03:32.390 --> 01:03:33.960
Then shoot!

01:03:33.960 --> 01:03:37.500
If you don't care if the professor's
wine bottle shatters, that is.

01:03:37.500 --> 01:03:38.830
B-Boy ...

01:03:45.110 --> 01:03:46.770
Conan-kun ...

01:04:03.520 --> 01:04:09.130
<i>Moriarty-sama</i> says he wishes to see you.

01:04:09.130 --> 01:04:10.970
Professor Moriarty does?!

01:04:10.970 --> 01:04:15.100
He waits in his carriage. Please follow me.

01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:16.590
P-Please wait!

01:04:18.870 --> 01:04:22.040
Do you intend to defy <i>Moriarty-sama?</i>

01:04:35.720 --> 01:04:37.890
I have brought them, Sir.

01:04:37.890 --> 01:04:39.390
Well done.

01:04:39.390 --> 01:04:42.530
Now then, boy. May I have that wine?

01:04:42.530 --> 01:04:43.860
Here.

01:04:46.070 --> 01:04:47.730
This scent ...

01:04:47.900 --> 01:04:49.400
You are indeed Holmes pupils,

01:04:49.400 --> 01:04:53.210
if you're able to fight on
even terms with Colonel Moran.

01:04:53.210 --> 01:04:56.210
So, you have business with me?

01:04:56.210 --> 01:04:59.810
Say, mister. You're Professor Moriarty?

01:04:59.810 --> 01:05:01.380
None other.

01:05:01.380 --> 01:05:05.820
Oh, I see. You're testing us.

01:05:05.820 --> 01:05:08.360
What do you mean?

01:05:08.360 --> 01:05:12.860
You can drop the act!
You're not Professor Moriarty, mister!

01:05:12.860 --> 01:05:15.900
W-What are you saying, <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

01:05:15.900 --> 01:05:19.560
After all, the real
Professor Moriarty is right here!

01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.840
- Eh?! He is?!
- Are you serious?!

01:05:24.840 --> 01:05:28.170
You used ventriloquism to
speak for him, didn't you?

01:05:31.850 --> 01:05:36.420
To think you saw through all
of that... How could you tell?

01:05:36.420 --> 01:05:40.790
Just now, Colonel Moran said,
"Please wait"! to you.

01:05:40.790 --> 01:05:46.060
Oh, right! Colonel Moran only
speaks politely to Professor Moriarty!

01:05:46.060 --> 01:05:47.760
Y-Yeah!

01:05:47.760 --> 01:05:49.460
Is that all?

01:05:49.460 --> 01:05:54.470
One other thing. I heard Professor
Moriarty was a fanciful old man

01:05:54.470 --> 01:05:56.640
who uses natural herbal cologne!

01:05:56.640 --> 01:06:01.410
Oh? And you smelled that
when you gave him the wine?

01:06:01.410 --> 01:06:05.400
Marvelously done. It's almost as
if I'm looking at a mini-Holmes.

01:06:07.920 --> 01:06:11.120
Incidentally, what business
do you have with me?

01:06:11.120 --> 01:06:14.120
You unleashed Jack the Ripper on the city

01:06:14.120 --> 01:06:18.060
to change London into a town of terror, right?

01:06:18.060 --> 01:06:20.560
That's not too far off the mark.

01:06:20.560 --> 01:06:25.730
Jack the Ripper was a vagabond boy
I found in the poor part of town.

01:06:25.730 --> 01:06:30.100
Abandoned by his mother,
he wandered the streets ...

01:06:30.100 --> 01:06:33.270
But I realized his talent the
moment I laid eyes on him.

01:06:33.270 --> 01:06:35.940
His talent as a criminal, that is.

01:06:38.150 --> 01:06:42.420
I raised him to be a
first-class professional killer.

01:06:42.420 --> 01:06:46.490
Why is he murdering innocent women?!

01:06:46.490 --> 01:06:49.760
Jack the Ripper became
more of a homicidal maniac

01:06:49.760 --> 01:06:51.930
than I had ever imagined.

01:06:51.930 --> 01:06:56.330
This string of murders is his own crazed doing.

01:06:56.330 --> 01:07:03.470
If you're trying to get rid of
Jack the Ripper, I'll lend you my help.

01:07:03.470 --> 01:07:04.940
Help?!

01:07:04.940 --> 01:07:08.780
Jack the Ripper has indeed begun to run wild,

01:07:08.780 --> 01:07:13.050
but he should still obey
my instructions to murder.

01:07:13.050 --> 01:07:16.180
You simply need to beat him to his target.

01:07:16.180 --> 01:07:17.720
How?!

01:07:17.720 --> 01:07:22.990
I will place a message for him in
the ads of tomorrow's Sunday Times.

01:07:22.990 --> 01:07:24.960
Who are you going to order him to kill?!

01:07:24.960 --> 01:07:27.620
You will find out in tomorrow's paper.

01:07:34.000 --> 01:07:37.670
Hey! Can we trust this old man?!

01:07:37.670 --> 01:07:39.660
Let's give it a shot.

01:07:40.970 --> 01:07:42.810
I pray for your luck.

01:07:42.810 --> 01:07:45.970
Be careful at the Reichenbach
Falls three years from now!

01:08:03.200 --> 01:08:05.570
What's "Reichenbach"?

01:08:05.570 --> 01:08:08.570
Three years from now,
Professor Moriarty and Holmes fight

01:08:08.570 --> 01:08:12.240
at the Reichenbach waterfall in Switzerland.

01:08:12.240 --> 01:08:14.780
They both fall to the bottom.

01:08:14.780 --> 01:08:18.050
Holmes miraculously survives,

01:08:18.050 --> 01:08:21.380
but Professor Moriarty supposedly dies.

01:08:21.380 --> 01:08:25.550
Why did I warn him like that?

01:08:25.550 --> 01:08:29.890
I guess maybe I like that
villain as much as Holmes does!

01:08:33.730 --> 01:08:35.720
That reminds me of that time ...

01:08:37.600 --> 01:08:40.270
I'm pretty fond of Professor Moriarty myself!

01:08:40.270 --> 01:08:43.940
Well, as a fictional character, anyway.

01:08:43.940 --> 01:08:48.210
Their confrontation at
Holmes house was mind-blowing!

01:08:48.210 --> 01:08:52.450
I just love one of the things Holmes said then!

01:08:52.450 --> 01:08:54.210
Can you guess what it is?

01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:55.650
No.

01:08:55.650 --> 01:08:57.310
It was ...

01:09:04.060 --> 01:09:08.060
What did Shinichi say?

01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:13.230
We were on a date, but he
kept talking about Holmes,

01:09:13.230 --> 01:09:14.890
so I tuned him out ...

01:09:16.900 --> 01:09:18.340
Hey, <i>Conan-kun.</i>

01:09:18.340 --> 01:09:20.110
Yeah?

01:09:20.110 --> 01:09:22.100
No. Never mind!

01:09:24.310 --> 01:09:29.680
I'm so dumb. Of course Conan-kun wouldn't know.

01:09:29.680 --> 01:09:32.650
H-Hey, Glasses.

01:09:32.650 --> 01:09:39.090
Sorry. It's our fault that four
people got a "game over" ...

01:09:39.090 --> 01:09:42.460
There's no point in worrying about what's done.

01:09:42.460 --> 01:09:47.300
I'd say the fact you've started to
think that way is a good step forward.

01:09:47.300 --> 01:09:52.300
Yes! Let's work hard to figure out
what to do next, for everyone!

01:10:08.860 --> 01:10:13.520
So this is where the second victim,
Honey Charleston, was found ...

01:10:31.750 --> 01:10:33.750
"The parent-child bazaar will be held again

01:10:33.750 --> 01:10:36.480
on the second Saturday in October."

01:10:36.480 --> 01:10:41.980
The second Saturday? As I recall,
Honey Charleston was killed ...

01:10:44.190 --> 01:10:46.180
... Saturday, September 8th!

01:10:53.070 --> 01:10:54.170
Sorry I made you wait!

01:10:54.170 --> 01:10:56.940
What took so long? Where were you?!

01:10:56.940 --> 01:10:59.210
Just exploring the city!

01:10:59.210 --> 01:11:02.510
You sure are carefree on
the day of our showdown.

01:11:02.510 --> 01:11:05.580
Jack the Ripper has struck again!

01:11:05.580 --> 01:11:07.950
There were two victims this time!

01:11:07.950 --> 01:11:09.280
I'll take a paper!

01:11:09.280 --> 01:11:10.920
Sure thing!

01:11:10.920 --> 01:11:13.720
Oh no! I don't have English money!

01:11:13.720 --> 01:11:16.220
Here you are! 80 yen!

01:11:16.220 --> 01:11:18.210
Oh. How convenient!

01:11:22.300 --> 01:11:23.730
Here it is!

01:11:23.730 --> 01:11:29.370
"Clean the opera house tonight. From M to J."

01:11:29.370 --> 01:11:31.040
"From M to J ..."

01:11:31.040 --> 01:11:33.540
"From Moriarty to Jack the Ripper."

01:11:33.540 --> 01:11:37.110
Clean the opera house? Is that his instruction?

01:11:37.110 --> 01:11:40.440
It could mean, "Murder an
actor who appears on stage ..."

01:11:42.280 --> 01:11:43.480
Here it is!

01:11:43.480 --> 01:11:44.920
"The Triumphant Performance Returns!

01:11:44.920 --> 01:11:48.790
Prima Donna in the Imperial
Opera of Warsaw ... Irene Adler!"

01:11:48.790 --> 01:11:53.260
Professor Moriarty!
You're the most despicable of villains!

01:11:53.260 --> 01:11:56.130
Who's Irene Adler?

01:11:56.130 --> 01:12:00.230
It's said she's the only
woman Holmes ever loved!

01:12:00.230 --> 01:12:03.730
Which means he made
Holmes beloved the murder target.

01:12:13.750 --> 01:12:15.920
12:06 A.M!

01:12:15.920 --> 01:12:19.250
- That means ...
all the other stages failed.

01:12:19.250 --> 01:12:22.920
Which means everyone's
lives are in the hands of us six!

01:12:41.370 --> 01:12:42.680
Hold it!

01:12:42.680 --> 01:12:46.450
This area is for authorized persons only!

01:12:46.450 --> 01:12:50.280
W-We're acquaintances of Irene <i>Adler-san!</i>

01:12:50.280 --> 01:12:52.120
We wanted to offer our
encouragement before she goes on!

01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:54.620
Oh! You know her?

01:12:54.620 --> 01:12:57.190
Yes! Where is her waiting room?

01:12:57.190 --> 01:13:00.520
In that case, it's the room at
the very end, with the poster.

01:13:02.230 --> 01:13:06.870
This must be it. I wonder
what she's like. I'm so excited!

01:13:06.870 --> 01:13:11.860
Given that my dad made her
character and that she's Holmes love ...

01:13:13.410 --> 01:13:14.740
Come in!

01:13:15.710 --> 01:13:17.370
Pardon the intrusion!

01:13:21.720 --> 01:13:23.980
Shinichi's mom!

01:13:23.980 --> 01:13:25.550
I knew it.

01:13:25.550 --> 01:13:29.220
How rude! I'm still single!

01:13:29.220 --> 01:13:33.430
Well, to be more precise,
I'm single now that I've divorced!

01:13:33.430 --> 01:13:35.500
A bouquet from <i>Holmes-san!</i>

01:13:35.500 --> 01:13:37.730
Oh! Thank you!

01:13:37.730 --> 01:13:39.700
Where might <i>Holmes-san</i> be?

01:13:39.700 --> 01:13:42.440
He was looking forward
to tonight's performance,

01:13:42.440 --> 01:13:44.870
but he had to leave on a case and can't come ...

01:13:44.870 --> 01:13:47.340
Oh. That's too bad.

01:13:47.340 --> 01:13:49.340
Please call tonight's show off!

01:13:49.340 --> 01:13:50.510
Eh?

01:13:50.510 --> 01:13:53.110
<i>Holmes-san's</i> arch-nemesis, Professor Moriarty,

01:13:53.110 --> 01:13:55.520
has sent someone to kill you!

01:13:55.520 --> 01:13:57.450
Why me?

01:13:57.450 --> 01:14:02.360
Because he wants to see
<i>Holmes-san's</i> sadness when he loses you!

01:14:02.360 --> 01:14:08.400
I'd like to see it, too! I wonder
how sad he would be for me ...

01:14:08.400 --> 01:14:13.200
You don't care about being
Jack the Ripper's fifth victim?!

01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:17.190
You're going to protect me, right?
In <i>Holmes-san's</i> place?

01:14:19.770 --> 01:14:22.940
Nothing scares this lady ...

01:14:22.940 --> 01:14:26.280
Yeah. This is exactly how she is ...

01:14:52.240 --> 01:14:56.570
Die beautifully, Irene Adler ...

01:14:59.750 --> 01:15:02.410
Where is he lurking?

01:15:12.090 --> 01:15:14.080
- What the...?!
- What's happening?!

01:15:17.930 --> 01:15:19.590
Look out!

01:15:23.640 --> 01:15:25.300
- Emori!
- <i>Takizawa-kun!</i>

01:15:27.510 --> 01:15:31.540
- Emori! You're...!
- You too, <i>Takizawa-kun!</i>

01:15:31.540 --> 01:15:33.210
Game over, huh ...

01:15:33.210 --> 01:15:35.520
This sucks ...

01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:38.180
Thank you. You saved my life!

01:15:41.020 --> 01:15:43.820
This is the first time
anyone's ever thanked me ...

01:15:43.820 --> 01:15:46.230
l-It feels nice!

01:15:46.230 --> 01:15:48.560
Moroboshi! I leave the rest to you now!

01:15:48.560 --> 01:15:50.550
You can count on me!

01:16:00.810 --> 01:16:02.800
- A-Akira!
- Shinya!

01:16:04.880 --> 01:16:08.540
That leaves only four,
including <i>Ran-kun</i> and <i>Conan-kun ...</i>

01:16:22.230 --> 01:16:27.720
That's it, Jack the Ripper!
Turn this world into Hell!

01:16:32.240 --> 01:16:34.840
Hurry! Out the back!

01:16:34.840 --> 01:16:36.610
Hurry, Haibara! That way!

01:16:36.610 --> 01:16:38.600
Conan! Look out!

01:16:44.850 --> 01:16:47.520
Haibara! Are you okay?!

01:16:47.520 --> 01:16:51.020
You can't give up, <i>Kudo-kun!</i>

01:16:51.020 --> 01:16:56.600
If there aren't any assist characters,
then you're our Holmes ...

01:16:56.600 --> 01:16:59.630
You're skilled enough for that.

01:16:59.630 --> 01:17:03.630
There's no case Holmes can't solve, right?

01:17:15.320 --> 01:17:16.300
<i>Ai-kun ...</i>

01:17:18.080 --> 01:17:20.420
Quickly! Quickly! Evacuate!

01:17:24.660 --> 01:17:26.320
Stay behind me!

01:17:36.400 --> 01:17:39.610
- Stop!
- Bye! You're safe with police around!

01:17:39.610 --> 01:17:42.740
Little boy! I still don't know your name!

01:17:42.740 --> 01:17:44.910
I'm Edogawa Conan!

01:17:44.910 --> 01:17:47.680
I have the same name as your guys birth father!

01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:49.340
Conan?

01:17:55.660 --> 01:17:57.650
I won't let him get away!

01:17:59.960 --> 01:18:01.260
How are things going?

01:18:01.260 --> 01:18:04.600
<i>Conan-kun's</i> group encountered Jack the Ripper.

01:18:04.600 --> 01:18:07.530
They're chasing him right now.

01:18:07.530 --> 01:18:09.370
Charing Cross Station!

01:18:27.820 --> 01:18:29.810
<i>Conan-kun!</i> Get on first!

01:18:34.630 --> 01:18:37.060
This is the worst possible scenario!

01:18:37.060 --> 01:18:39.400
How so?

01:18:39.400 --> 01:18:42.870
The last train out of Charing Cross Station ...

01:18:42.870 --> 01:18:44.860
It's the most dangerous climax of all!

01:19:01.190 --> 01:19:06.390
Eh?! Jack the Ripper is
disguised as a passenger?!

01:19:06.390 --> 01:19:08.830
Please gather all the
passengers onto a single car!

01:19:08.830 --> 01:19:10.160
R-Right!

01:19:18.770 --> 01:19:20.430
Mr. Conductor! Could you ...

01:19:22.510 --> 01:19:25.510
Okay, everyone! Please raise both hands!

01:19:25.510 --> 01:19:29.170
I want to make sure no
one is carrying a weapon.

01:19:36.090 --> 01:19:39.750
I look forward to hearing you figure this out ...

01:19:40.530 --> 01:19:45.800
I'll now explain what was
written in Mr. Holmes notes.

01:19:45.800 --> 01:19:51.100
Honey Charleston, the second
victim of Jack the Ripper,

01:19:51.100 --> 01:19:55.540
was married in the town of Windsor,
but as she was full of dreams,

01:19:55.540 --> 01:20:00.080
she abandoned her husband and son
10 years ago to come to London.

01:20:00.080 --> 01:20:04.780
These two rings were at the scene
of Honey Charleston's murder.

01:20:04.780 --> 01:20:06.250
One is Honey's.

01:20:06.250 --> 01:20:11.490
The other has the same design,
but didn't fit any of Honey's fingers.

01:20:11.490 --> 01:20:14.930
So Mr. Holmes believes the following.

01:20:14.930 --> 01:20:18.930
He thinks these two rings may
have signified the parent-child bond

01:20:18.930 --> 01:20:22.340
between the victim,
Honey Charleston, and Jack the Ripper.

01:20:22.340 --> 01:20:26.310
Meaning that little ring is Jack the Ripper's?!

01:20:26.310 --> 01:20:27.570
Yes.

01:20:27.570 --> 01:20:31.740
She put a ring of the same design
on her son's finger before leaving.

01:20:31.740 --> 01:20:35.950
Does that mean Jack the Ripper
murdered his own mother?

01:20:35.950 --> 01:20:39.950
Yeah. According to his notes,
the day she was murdered, Sept. 8,

01:20:39.950 --> 01:20:41.960
was the second Saturday of September,

01:20:41.960 --> 01:20:45.960
the day of the monthly bazaar
at the Whitechapel church,

01:20:45.960 --> 01:20:51.200
in which parents and children
bring things they made together!

01:20:51.200 --> 01:20:54.670
And he thinks Jack the Ripper knew that!

01:20:54.670 --> 01:20:58.140
Eh? He even wrote that down?

01:20:58.140 --> 01:21:04.540
In other words, Jack the Ripper
wanted to participate with his mother,

01:21:04.540 --> 01:21:06.780
so he left their two rings?

01:21:06.780 --> 01:21:09.450
Yeah! Apparently!

01:21:09.450 --> 01:21:14.440
Then his motive was his grudge
for his mother abandoning him ...

01:21:15.790 --> 01:21:19.450
What did I do?! I'm not the only one drunk!

01:21:22.960 --> 01:21:27.460
But his bloodlust was almost out of love ...

01:21:29.840 --> 01:21:32.370
How sad ...

01:21:32.370 --> 01:21:35.910
Apparently, he chose an unrelated
woman for his first victim

01:21:35.910 --> 01:21:38.810
to throw the police off.

01:21:38.810 --> 01:21:42.150
But what about the third and fourth victims?

01:21:42.150 --> 01:21:44.880
Professor Moriarty's special education

01:21:44.880 --> 01:21:49.260
molded Jack the Ripper
into a psychotic criminal,

01:21:49.260 --> 01:21:51.660
so even after clearing his
grudge with his mother,

01:21:51.660 --> 01:21:56.620
he couldn't help but continue
targeting women like her.

01:21:56.900 --> 01:21:58.830
Who is it, then?!

01:21:58.830 --> 01:22:03.840
If he kept the ring on since childhood,

01:22:03.840 --> 01:22:06.840
what do you think would happen to his finger?

01:22:06.840 --> 01:22:11.170
Out of his 10 fingers, that
one finger should be thin!

01:22:14.850 --> 01:22:17.840
Jack the Ripper is you!

01:22:20.950 --> 01:22:22.940
But that's a woman!

01:22:26.260 --> 01:22:28.250
Her right ring finger is thin!

01:22:36.600 --> 01:22:38.590
- I got this!
- No! <i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:22:41.040 --> 01:22:42.710
Damn! A smokescreen!

01:22:42.710 --> 01:22:44.700
- Open the window!
- Yeah!

01:22:52.620 --> 01:22:53.950
T-They're gone!

01:22:53.950 --> 01:22:55.610
H-Hey!

01:22:58.060 --> 01:23:01.390
All the passengers have
disappeared! What's going on?!

01:23:06.430 --> 01:23:11.670
Now, then. Let us identify
who Kashimura's killer was, too.

01:23:11.670 --> 01:23:14.770
Eh?! You know who did it?!

01:23:14.770 --> 01:23:19.910
The issue is how the killer
prepared the murder weapon.

01:23:19.910 --> 01:23:25.350
A metal detector is installed at
the entrance to the Beika City Hall.

01:23:25.350 --> 01:23:32.130
So it's mostly likely that the weapon
was already inside the building.

01:23:32.130 --> 01:23:35.330
But where could someone get that?!

01:23:35.330 --> 01:23:38.660
The bronze statues in the party hall.

01:23:38.660 --> 01:23:41.330
One of them is holding a dagger.

01:23:43.300 --> 01:23:46.540
The party hall was filled with guests!

01:23:46.540 --> 01:23:49.440
Someone would've seen the killer taking it!

01:23:49.440 --> 01:23:56.350
It was removed when the lights went out.
It had all been scheduled.

01:23:56.350 --> 01:24:01.120
But wouldn't someone have
noticed the dagger was missing?!

01:24:01.120 --> 01:24:06.960
A fake was left in its place.
Made of cardboard and foil or something.

01:24:06.960 --> 01:24:10.000
Then, is the dagger the statue's holding now

01:24:10.000 --> 01:24:12.300
the one used in the murder?!

01:24:12.300 --> 01:24:18.640
Yes. I just had a luminol test and
fingerprint check done on the dagger.

01:24:18.640 --> 01:24:22.410
Blood the same type as Kashimura's was found.

01:24:22.410 --> 01:24:26.550
Fingerprints were also found on the handle.

01:24:26.550 --> 01:24:31.980
Your fingerprints, President Schindler.

01:24:31.980 --> 01:24:37.190
Of course they were. The bronze
statues were brought from my home.

01:24:37.190 --> 01:24:40.190
This is surveillance footage of the party hall

01:24:40.190 --> 01:24:43.560
from before and after the incident.

01:24:43.560 --> 01:24:48.170
Luckily, surveillance cameras
are placed all around the hall,

01:24:48.170 --> 01:24:52.000
so I could record from every angle.

01:24:52.000 --> 01:24:55.070
The ball that young Moroboshi
kicks hits the bronze statue

01:24:55.070 --> 01:24:58.040
and knocks the dagger off.

01:24:58.040 --> 01:25:02.550
He picks it up and returns
it to the statue's hand.

01:25:02.550 --> 01:25:06.050
I see! If the dagger shown here is the real one,

01:25:06.050 --> 01:25:09.020
the boy's fingerprints should be on it too!

01:25:09.020 --> 01:25:14.090
But only President Schindler's
fingerprints were found!

01:25:14.090 --> 01:25:19.130
I simply touched it after the boy,
so his fingerprints are gone.

01:25:19.130 --> 01:25:22.200
<i>Kudo-sensei!</i> I found it!

01:25:22.200 --> 01:25:24.640
There was a fake dagger
made of cardboard and foil

01:25:24.640 --> 01:25:26.140
in the basement garbage collection!

01:25:26.140 --> 01:25:27.810
Any fingerprints?!

01:25:27.810 --> 01:25:30.040
It's just like you said, <i>Kudo-sensei!</i>

01:25:30.040 --> 01:25:36.080
It has young Moroboshi's and
President Schindler's fingerprints!

01:25:36.080 --> 01:25:41.050
The only fingerprints that can be
on the fake dagger besides the boy's

01:25:41.050 --> 01:25:43.090
are the killer's.

01:25:43.090 --> 01:25:47.130
This is a set-up! I'm issuing a
protest to the Japanese government!

01:25:47.130 --> 01:25:50.460
Besides, I have no reason to
murder Kashimura in the first place!

01:25:54.430 --> 01:25:57.430
They're not here! All that's
up ahead is the engine room!

01:26:04.840 --> 01:26:06.680
The driver is gone!

01:26:06.680 --> 01:26:09.010
- We gotta stop the train!
- Yeah!

01:26:11.250 --> 01:26:13.240
The brake's been destroyed!

01:26:22.630 --> 01:26:24.300
We're speeding up!

01:26:24.300 --> 01:26:27.830
Hey! Shouldn't we find that girl?!

01:26:27.830 --> 01:26:31.140
Ran! Where are you?! Where did you go?!

01:26:31.140 --> 01:26:32.800
Wait!

01:26:34.340 --> 01:26:36.330
There they are!

01:26:43.620 --> 01:26:45.180
<i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:26:45.180 --> 01:26:47.180
No! Stay away!

01:26:49.160 --> 01:26:52.330
I've tied myself to this girl.

01:26:52.330 --> 01:26:56.130
If I fall, she comes with me!

01:26:56.130 --> 01:26:58.660
So, how will you fight?!

01:26:58.660 --> 01:27:00.330
Dammit!

01:27:01.470 --> 01:27:04.470
I hear the statue's dagger
has been passed down

01:27:04.470 --> 01:27:08.540
from generation to generation in
the same Schindler family bloodline.

01:27:08.540 --> 01:27:11.240
Indeed it has.

01:27:11.240 --> 01:27:15.410
Why did you use it as the murder weapon?

01:27:15.410 --> 01:27:21.410
Assuming you didn't have to
use it as the murder weapon ...

01:27:25.360 --> 01:27:28.360
What is it you want, Jack the Ripper?!

01:27:28.360 --> 01:27:30.160
"Want"?!

01:27:30.160 --> 01:27:33.370
Now that you've killed your mother
and cleared your long grudge,

01:27:33.370 --> 01:27:35.170
what is it you want?!

01:27:35.170 --> 01:27:37.170
To continue living!

01:27:37.170 --> 01:27:40.170
I'm going to let the vicious
blood flowing through my veins

01:27:40.170 --> 01:27:43.840
survive to the next
generation aboard Noah's boat!

01:27:47.350 --> 01:27:50.010
I take it this is your motive
for murdering Kashimura.

01:27:52.220 --> 01:27:57.390
Almost as if he had been aboard
Noah's ark, Jack the Ripper's blood

01:27:57.390 --> 01:28:00.730
survived to the present day.

01:28:00.730 --> 01:28:04.560
You're Jack the Ripper's descendant.

01:28:04.560 --> 01:28:08.200
- J-Jack the Ripper's ...
- ... descendant?!

01:28:08.200 --> 01:28:13.040
<i>Hiroki-kun</i> most likely learned
this using his DNA Search Program.

01:28:13.040 --> 01:28:17.040
If the world learned that the czar
of the IT industry is the descendant

01:28:17.040 --> 01:28:21.980
of the psychotic serial murderer
from 100 years ago, he'd be done for.

01:28:21.980 --> 01:28:25.890
So, to keep things quiet,
you drove <i>Hiroki-kun</i> to suicide ...

01:28:25.890 --> 01:28:29.890
... and murdered Kashimura!

01:28:29.890 --> 01:28:34.880
It was when Hiroki came to see my collection.

01:28:36.630 --> 01:28:41.400
This is a gold wine cup used
by the Egyptian king Khufu.

01:28:41.400 --> 01:28:44.240
Next is Ganjin Wajo's scriptures

01:28:44.240 --> 01:28:48.810
and the manuscript of Edogawa
Rampo's "The Psychological Test."

01:28:48.810 --> 01:28:50.140
Amazing!

01:28:51.980 --> 01:28:54.450
What about this dagger?

01:28:54.450 --> 01:28:57.780
Oh, uhh ...

01:28:57.780 --> 01:29:00.790
It's supposedly the weapon
used by Jack the Ripper,

01:29:00.790 --> 01:29:03.420
a deranged serial killer from a century ago ...

01:29:03.420 --> 01:29:06.410
There's no telling if it really is, though.

01:29:10.460 --> 01:29:16.040
For an experiment, Hiroki gathered
all the data around him he could

01:29:16.040 --> 01:29:18.670
and entered it into the computer.

01:29:18.670 --> 01:29:22.980
And the DNA of Honey Charleston,
taken from the dagger,

01:29:22.980 --> 01:29:25.850
matched with yours.

01:29:25.850 --> 01:29:27.980
You were afraid.

01:29:27.980 --> 01:29:30.980
Afraid that <i>Hiroki-kun</i> would eventually learn

01:29:30.980 --> 01:29:33.390
that Jack the Ripper was Honey's son.

01:29:33.390 --> 01:29:36.290
Afraid it was only a matter
of time until he learned

01:29:36.290 --> 01:29:39.460
you're Jack the Ripper's descendant!

01:29:39.460 --> 01:29:44.330
I was scared of the terrifying
blood that flows inside me!

01:29:44.330 --> 01:29:48.470
Who cares about your
"murderer's blood" or the public eye?!

01:29:48.470 --> 01:29:51.130
Why didn't you try to fight it?!

01:29:54.340 --> 01:29:57.710
Just as <i>Conan-kun</i> and his friends are now.

01:29:57.710 --> 01:29:59.310
Thomas Schindler.

01:29:59.310 --> 01:30:02.300
You're under arrest for the
murder of Kashimura <i>Tadaaki-san.</i>

01:30:15.330 --> 01:30:18.700
You'll never catch me if
you're always running away!

01:30:18.700 --> 01:30:21.500
10 minutes until the final stop.

01:30:21.500 --> 01:30:24.490
What do you think will happen
to this train, without its driver?

01:30:30.680 --> 01:30:33.670
Though it seems you'll be long
dead before the next station.

01:30:36.880 --> 01:30:38.870
<i>Conan-kun!</i> Behind you!

01:30:47.260 --> 01:30:49.590
End of the line, boy.

01:30:50.800 --> 01:30:52.360
<i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:30:52.360 --> 01:30:54.070
Let Glasses go!

01:30:54.070 --> 01:30:55.730
<i>Moroboshi-kun!</i>

01:30:57.370 --> 01:30:58.370
Are you all right?!

01:30:58.370 --> 01:31:01.770
I-I think!

01:31:01.770 --> 01:31:04.770
Now then! Where shall I start carving from?

01:31:07.980 --> 01:31:09.920
What do I do?!

01:31:09.920 --> 01:31:13.250
Shinichi! What would you do in this situation?!

01:31:14.550 --> 01:31:19.120
I just love one of the things Holmes said then!

01:31:19.120 --> 01:31:20.560
Can you guess what it is?

01:31:20.560 --> 01:31:22.390
No.

01:31:22.390 --> 01:31:27.400
It was, "If you precise destruction,

01:31:27.400 --> 01:31:31.060
in the public interest,
I am willing to accept death."

01:31:35.840 --> 01:31:37.580
Glasses!

01:31:37.580 --> 01:31:40.570
The Reichenbach Falls, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:31:44.680 --> 01:31:46.450
Don't tell me you're?!

01:31:46.450 --> 01:31:49.790
I'm sorry I couldn't be with you to the end.

01:31:52.020 --> 01:31:53.830
Stop! Ran!

01:31:53.830 --> 01:31:55.490
Damn it!

01:32:01.270 --> 01:32:02.930
Crap!

01:32:06.470 --> 01:32:09.460
Conan-kun, I believe in you.

01:32:22.450 --> 01:32:24.450
Ran!

01:32:28.360 --> 01:32:30.690
Glasses! We have to stop the train!

01:32:33.030 --> 01:32:36.370
Hey! We have to stop the
train so we can survive!

01:32:36.370 --> 01:32:40.310
We still haven't won the game!

01:32:40.310 --> 01:32:41.870
Get up, Glasses!

01:32:41.870 --> 01:32:44.680
The lives of 48 people are in our hands!

01:32:44.680 --> 01:32:47.650
Are you just going to trample all over them?!

01:32:47.650 --> 01:32:49.980
Don't be stupid! I don't wanna give up, either!

01:32:52.720 --> 01:32:57.320
Think about it. The train
is continually speeding up.

01:32:57.320 --> 01:32:59.590
It's moving at approximately 100 kph.

01:32:59.590 --> 01:33:02.490
It'll reach the station in under five minutes.

01:33:02.490 --> 01:33:04.330
The only way to save everyone

01:33:04.330 --> 01:33:08.900
was to cut the links connecting the
engine car and the passenger cars!

01:33:08.900 --> 01:33:13.510
With just us two, those
links won't budge at all!

01:33:13.510 --> 01:33:20.710
Yes. I was specifically counting
on Ran to help us with it ...

01:33:20.710 --> 01:33:25.550
That's why Noah's Ark got
rid of all the passengers.

01:33:25.550 --> 01:33:28.540
It's all over. There's nothing more we can do.

01:33:31.520 --> 01:33:33.960
It's all over, Dad ...

01:33:33.960 --> 01:33:36.300
Hey, now! Don't give up!

01:33:36.300 --> 01:33:41.530
You gotta survive and let Ran live again!

01:33:41.530 --> 01:33:42.860
Shinichi ...

01:33:50.380 --> 01:33:55.950
You still aren't covered in blood yet.
You're still alive.

01:33:55.950 --> 01:33:57.980
Are you giving up already?

01:33:57.980 --> 01:34:01.320
Just when you have both hands
on the string to unravel the truth?

01:34:07.960 --> 01:34:09.960
The crimson red string of murder

01:34:09.960 --> 01:34:14.170
has been mixed in the bundle
of colorless threads of life.

01:34:14.170 --> 01:34:18.740
Isn't disentangling that what we do?

01:34:18.740 --> 01:34:20.400
Holmes!

01:34:24.110 --> 01:34:28.010
Wasn't he in Dartmoor? Could it be a bug?

01:34:28.010 --> 01:34:29.850
What does he mean?

01:34:29.850 --> 01:34:34.620
Jack the Ripper is dead, so why do
we have to get covered in blood?

01:34:34.620 --> 01:34:37.190
This is it! This is what he meant!

01:34:37.190 --> 01:34:38.420
The freight car!

01:34:38.420 --> 01:34:40.360
Hey! Wait! What do you mean?!

01:34:40.360 --> 01:34:42.350
Just come on!

01:34:47.630 --> 01:34:51.340
Use that axe to break the red wine barrels!

01:34:51.340 --> 01:34:52.670
Hurry!

01:35:09.450 --> 01:35:11.790
- Dive under on my signal!
- Okay!

01:35:25.640 --> 01:35:26.970
Now!

01:36:00.670 --> 01:36:02.210
Have they said anything?!

01:36:02.210 --> 01:36:04.610
Still nothing!

01:36:04.610 --> 01:36:08.100
Oh wonderful, merciful <i>Conan-sama!</i>
I beg of you to save Ran!

01:36:19.860 --> 01:36:22.690
I see. "Covered in blood".

01:36:22.690 --> 01:36:28.030
It meant, "Use the red
wine to cushion the shock".

01:36:28.030 --> 01:36:32.600
Thanks for the help, Holmes. No... Dad.

01:36:32.600 --> 01:36:37.740
You're awake, Glasses? It seems you win.

01:36:37.740 --> 01:36:39.070
"You"?

01:36:42.780 --> 01:36:44.770
So I was right.

01:36:46.820 --> 01:36:50.960
I'm glad I trusted you. Thank you.

01:36:50.960 --> 01:36:55.760
You're welcome ... Noah's Ark.

01:36:55.760 --> 01:36:59.400
Or should I call you <i>Hiroki-kun?</i>

01:36:59.400 --> 01:37:03.730
You borrowed <i>Moroboshi-kun's</i>
data to join in the game too, right?

01:37:08.310 --> 01:37:11.180
When did you realize it?

01:37:11.180 --> 01:37:16.180
There's no need to worry. I've cut
communication with the real world.

01:37:16.180 --> 01:37:20.990
The first thing that
seemed strange was Big Ben!

01:37:20.990 --> 01:37:24.190
You noticed it before the clock hand moved.

01:37:24.190 --> 01:37:29.760
You did that to tell us what
Big Ben's time indicated, right?

01:37:29.760 --> 01:37:31.760
Next was the soccer ball.

01:37:31.760 --> 01:37:35.800
You called it a filthy ball
and threw it behind you.

01:37:35.800 --> 01:37:37.600
A 100 year-old soccer ball

01:37:37.600 --> 01:37:41.270
would've been very interesting
to any soccer-loving boy.

01:37:43.810 --> 01:37:47.810
I'm guessing that
although you put us in danger,

01:37:47.810 --> 01:37:52.990
you had faith we would overcome it as a group.

01:37:52.990 --> 01:37:57.690
You didn't need to kill the next
few generations to reset Japan.

01:37:57.690 --> 01:38:01.690
You hoped that overcoming
obstacles, the game's in this case,

01:38:01.690 --> 01:38:06.800
without our parents help would
help us mature on our own, right?

01:38:06.800 --> 01:38:08.830
You weren't able to be heartless!

01:38:08.830 --> 01:38:12.370
Holmes appearance at the end is the proof.

01:38:12.370 --> 01:38:16.710
You let the assist character
show up right at the climax!

01:38:19.750 --> 01:38:23.850
I borrowed <i>Moroboshi-kun's</i>
body and snuck into the game

01:38:23.850 --> 01:38:28.550
because I wanted to play
with friends at least once.

01:38:28.550 --> 01:38:33.660
I was always busy working, you see ...

01:38:33.660 --> 01:38:40.930
I'm sorry for frightening you.
But I had so much fun!

01:38:40.930 --> 01:38:43.940
And, I was jealous of how you and your dad

01:38:43.940 --> 01:38:49.880
can communicate with your
minds even if you're far apart!

01:38:49.880 --> 01:38:56.520
Your dad avenged my dad's killer. Thank you!

01:38:56.520 --> 01:39:00.590
It's time to say goodbye.

01:39:00.590 --> 01:39:05.580
Your mind will continue to
live on in Noah's Ark, right?

01:39:07.930 --> 01:39:10.430
As long as computers like me are alive,

01:39:10.430 --> 01:39:14.070
grownups will use them for bad things.

01:39:14.070 --> 01:39:17.060
It was still too soon to
create an artificial brain ...

01:39:19.910 --> 01:39:23.780
Okay! Return to your world!

01:39:23.780 --> 01:39:27.980
After you wake up, I want
everyone to at least know this:

01:39:27.980 --> 01:39:32.310
Real life isn't easy, like it is in video games.

01:39:40.890 --> 01:39:43.550
I hope you see your father!

01:39:46.970 --> 01:39:48.930
Goodbye ...

01:39:48.930 --> 01:39:50.600
... Kudo Shinichi.

01:40:33.980 --> 01:40:35.980
Ran!

01:40:35.980 --> 01:40:37.970
Looks like he did it!

01:40:55.070 --> 01:40:57.970
- Thank goodness you're all right!
- That was fun!

01:40:57.970 --> 01:40:59.960
- I worked hard!
- Good job!

01:41:04.080 --> 01:41:07.550
<i>Conan-kun!</i> Thanks for bringing us back to life!

01:41:07.550 --> 01:41:09.810
We worked pretty hard, didn't we?!

01:41:09.810 --> 01:41:11.810
That was an incredible adventure!

01:41:14.190 --> 01:41:17.180
Reality really is much better ...

01:41:20.760 --> 01:41:22.250
What happened?

01:41:27.170 --> 01:41:30.100
I knew you'd be able to do it, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:41:30.100 --> 01:41:34.740
But, <i>Ran-neechan!</i> Jumping off
with him was way too crazy!

01:41:34.740 --> 01:41:39.010
But I remembered one of
Shinichi's favorite Holmes quotes!

01:41:39.010 --> 01:41:44.850
Eh? Was it when Holmes and
Prof. Moriarty met for the first time?

01:41:44.850 --> 01:41:47.550
Huh? How do you know that?

01:41:47.550 --> 01:41:51.690
No, uhh, I heard from <i>Shinichi-niichan,</i> too ...

01:41:51.690 --> 01:41:57.560
Oh! But all his blabbing
really proved useful for once!

01:41:57.560 --> 01:42:01.370
Stop calling it "blabbing"!

01:42:01.370 --> 01:42:04.200
- Ran!
- Dad!

01:42:04.200 --> 01:42:06.190
Thank goodness you're okay!

01:42:26.120 --> 01:42:29.260
That took a bit long for you.

01:42:29.260 --> 01:42:31.590
Yeah. I quite enjoyed it.

01:42:47.080 --> 01:42:52.080
Noah's Ark is ending his own life.

01:42:52.080 --> 01:42:55.580
Rest in peace, <i>Hiroki-kun.</i>

01:43:15.350 --> 01:43:20.820
What kind of things happened today?

01:43:15.350 --> 01:43:20.820
kyou wa donna koto ga atta no?

01:43:21.940 --> 01:43:27.120
May tomorrow end without incident, too

01:43:21.940 --> 01:43:27.120
asu mo buji ni owaru you ni

01:43:27.400 --> 01:43:33.420
No matter what does or doesn't happen,

01:43:27.400 --> 01:43:33.420
nani ga okite mo okoranakute mo

01:43:34.120 --> 01:43:45.390
those skies will continue moving ahead

01:43:34.120 --> 01:43:45.390
ano sora wa susumi tsudzukeru

01:43:47.260 --> 01:43:52.940
From the moment I met you

01:43:47.260 --> 01:43:52.940
kimi ni deaeta sono toki kara

01:43:53.710 --> 01:44:00.030
every single second has been very precious

01:43:53.710 --> 01:44:00.030
ichibyou zutsu ga totemo daiji na nda

01:44:00.310 --> 01:44:06.870
These everlasting feelings will continue forever

01:44:00.310 --> 01:44:06.870
itsu made mo togirenu omoi

01:44:12.530 --> 01:44:18.420
Even on the most uneasy of days

01:44:12.530 --> 01:44:18.420
dou ni mo fuan de shikatanai hi mo

01:44:19.370 --> 01:44:24.640
you can't show your faintheartedness to anyone

01:44:19.370 --> 01:44:24.640
dare ni mo yowane wo hakenai ndaro

01:44:24.910 --> 01:44:31.140
Amid a tangled mess of strings,

01:44:24.910 --> 01:44:31.140
ikutsu mono ito motsureau naka

01:44:31.430 --> 01:44:42.450
we're connected

01:44:31.430 --> 01:44:42.450
bokutachi wa tsunagatte iru

01:44:44.430 --> 01:44:50.330
I remember your warmth

01:44:44.430 --> 01:44:50.330
kimi no nukumori oboe teru yo

01:44:50.860 --> 01:44:57.300
That straightforward voice still rings in my ears, too

01:44:50.860 --> 01:44:57.300
sono massugu na koe mo hibii teru yo

01:44:57.580 --> 01:45:04.220
These everlasting feelings will continue forever

01:44:57.580 --> 01:45:04.220
itsu made mo togirenu omoi

01:45:07.460 --> 01:45:13.650
Rescue that bond that's about to be buried in the darkness

01:45:07.460 --> 01:45:13.650
yami ni umoresou na kizuna wo torimodose

01:45:33.570 --> 01:45:39.420
From the moment I met you

01:45:33.570 --> 01:45:39.420
kimi ni deaeta sono toki kara

01:45:40.200 --> 01:45:46.390
I've felt that I'm not alone anymore

01:45:40.200 --> 01:45:46.390
mou hitori janai to omoeta nda

01:45:46.670 --> 01:45:52.520
I can keep on living now

01:45:46.670 --> 01:45:52.520
kimi ga doka ka de miteru nda to

01:45:53.010 --> 01:45:59.480
with the feeling that you're watching from somewhere

01:45:53.010 --> 01:45:59.480
omoi nagara zutto ikite ikeru yo

01:45:59.770 --> 01:46:05.780
These everlasting feelings will continue forever

01:45:59.770 --> 01:46:05.780
itsu made mo togirenu omoi

01:46:06.310 --> 01:46:13.870
These never-ending feelings will reach out forever

01:46:06.310 --> 01:46:13.870
doko made mo taenai omoi

01:47:00.000 --> 01:47:02.990
Gotta practice up so I won't
get made fun of anymore ...
